00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:43.170
Freddy lures Tina into an alley using a mysterious voice.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.434
Then, after rolling a trash can lid in her direction to startle her, reveals

00:14:46.482 --> 00:14:50.186
his horrifying appearance, arms extended unnaturally to scrape the wall with

00:14:50.208 --> 00:14:51.062
his bladed glove.

00:14:51.126 --> 00:14:53.194
Tina's first reaction is to seek help in god.

00:14:53.232 --> 00:14:56.826
But Freddy, persistently in opposition to religion, mocks her god with his response. 

00:14:57.963 --> 00:14:58.834
–[Tina] Please God!

00:14:58.834 --> 00:15:01.790
–[Freddy] THIS is God.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.906
He chases her back to the house, demonstrating the ability to warp around

00:15:04.928 --> 00:15:07.982
the dream scene, slice off his own fingers with no pain, and have his face

00:15:08.036 --> 00:15:08.638
torn away.

00:15:08.724 --> 00:15:11.454
Remember, he's been doing this for some time at this point, and has already

00:15:11.492 --> 00:15:13.914
developed tricks to terrify and torture his victims using dream logic.

00:15:13.962 --> 00:15:17.214
He pins her down and slashes her through the chest before

00:15:17.252 --> 00:15:19.458
dragging and tossing her body all around the room.

00:15:19.544 --> 00:15:22.814
The others are woken up by the commotion and don't manage to get any sleep

00:15:22.862 --> 00:15:23.822
after seeing the scene.

00:15:23.886 --> 00:15:27.326
So it isn't until the next day that Freddy is able to target Nancy, who falls

00:15:27.358 --> 00:15:28.306
asleep in class.

00:15:28.408 --> 00:15:31.714
Freddy is able to manipulate the dreams of his victims, so he causes Nancy

00:15:31.762 --> 00:15:34.866
to see her best friend in a body bag, the first in a trail of breadcrumbs

00:15:34.898 --> 00:15:36.182
that he uses to draw her in.

00:15:36.236 --> 00:15:38.998
He shape shifts into a hall monitor, who she runs into on her way to the basement,

00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:41.942
which turns out to be none other than Freddy's boiler room.

00:15:41.996 --> 00:15:44.146
The school basement never disappoints in a horror movie.

00:15:44.178 --> 00:15:46.966
I remember when I was in high school, on one of the last days, I was just

00:15:46.988 --> 00:15:50.046
walking around, not in class, and I saw the principal walking around and

00:15:50.108 --> 00:15:52.686
asked him to show me the basement, the one place in the school that I had

00:15:52.708 --> 00:15:53.208
never seen.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:53.774
And he did.

00:15:53.812 --> 00:15:55.550
He didn't even question why I wasn't in class.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:59.214
And it just goes to show, sometimes you just gotta ask for things,

00:15:59.252 --> 00:16:00.186
Like asking you to subscribe.

00:16:00.218 --> 00:16:03.246
Freddy emerges from behind the boiler and slices his own chest, just as he

00:16:03.268 --> 00:16:04.014
used to as a boy.

00:16:04.052 --> 00:16:06.474
But this time, it reveals maggots and green ooze.

00:16:06.522 --> 00:16:08.666
He laughs maniacally as he chases her around.

00:16:08.708 --> 00:16:12.146
But unlike Tina, Nancy manages to wake herself up at the end by reaching for

00:16:12.168 --> 00:16:12.862
a hot pipe.

00:16:12.926 --> 00:16:15.938
But thanks to the power given to him by the dream demons, any injuries that

00:16:15.944 --> 00:16:18.514
he dishes out in dreams also carry through to real life.

00:16:18.552 --> 00:16:21.062
And Nancy wakes up realizing that the burn is real.

00:16:21.116 --> 00:16:24.006
Not to be deterred, Freddy continues to haunt Nancy's dreams whenever she falls asleep,

00:16:24.028 --> 00:16:27.046
like when she dozes off in the bathtub and he pulls her under the surface, 

00:16:27.068 --> 00:16:30.038
once again hinting at that metaphor that the studio didn't want

00:16:30.044 --> 00:16:30.498
to include blatantly.

00:16:30.498 --> 00:16:34.026
In another dream, Freddy visits Rod, who's being held in jail as

00:16:34.048 --> 00:16:35.254
a suspect in Tina's death.

00:16:35.302 --> 00:16:38.154
He gives chase, continuing to use images of Tina to torture her.

00:16:38.192 --> 00:16:41.574
But ultimately Nancy's alarm clock saves her, perhaps wanting an easier target,

00:16:41.622 --> 00:16:45.146
or perhaps realizing it'll have a psychological effect on Nancy if

00:16:45.168 --> 00:16:46.442
another one of her friends dies.

00:16:46.506 --> 00:16:49.758
Freddy turns his efforts to Rod, kills him in his dream and stages it as a suicide. 

00:16:49.764 --> 00:16:52.254
He goes for another round with Nancy after this.

00:16:52.292 --> 00:16:55.230
However, I don't have the details because we see this dream from an outside

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:58.590
perspective while Nancy is being studied at the Katja Sleep Institute.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:01.618
However, it must have been pretty traumatic because she wakes up with a

00:17:01.624 --> 00:17:05.490
fresh trio of cuts on her arm, a strand of gray hair and a souvenir.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:07.490
– [Nancy] I brought something out from my dream.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.722
At some point the next night, Freddy calls the phone in her bedroom.

00:17:10.786 --> 00:17:13.830
She's expecting to hear from her boyfriend Glen, but it turns out to be

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.400
more of a nuisance call.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.290
–[Freddy] I’m your boyfriend now, Nancy!

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:20.386
A tongue protrudes out of the receiver and licks her, causing her to spike

00:17:20.418 --> 00:17:21.542
the phone and destroy it.

00:17:21.596 --> 00:17:24.298
That's still preferred to getting a telemarketer though.

00:17:24.304 --> 00:17:26.566
It wouldn't be the last time that Freddy used his tongue to freak out a victim.

00:17:26.598 --> 00:17:29.382
And it all ties into the inappropriate subtext of his character.

00:17:29.446 --> 00:17:31.402
But Nancy isn't even asleep for this.

00:17:31.456 --> 00:17:34.846
So how did Freddy get to her in the waking world?

00:17:34.868 --> 00:17:35.594
At this point, Nancy is running out empty.

00:17:35.642 --> 00:17:38.606
She's mostly stayed awake twenty four seven for the last few days, and her

00:17:38.628 --> 00:17:39.754
body really needs sleep.

00:17:39.802 --> 00:17:42.874
There's something called hypnogogic hallucination, also known as waking dreams.

00:17:42.922 --> 00:17:46.026
These are brief hallucinations that take place as you're falling asleep.

00:17:46.058 --> 00:17:48.590
They can be visual, auditory or physical.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.702
You may have experienced this in a minor capacity.

00:17:50.766 --> 00:17:53.598
You're about to fall asleep and you hear someone say your name, but there's

00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:54.242
nobody there.

00:17:54.296 --> 00:17:56.686
Or you hear your phone buzz, but there's no notification.

00:17:56.798 --> 00:17:59.714
Now that I've looked into hypnogogic hallucination, I actually think it may

00:17:59.752 --> 00:18:01.634
explain a mystery that's always haunted me.

00:18:01.672 --> 00:18:04.658
I used to do production sound for movies and video, and in one indie film

00:18:04.674 --> 00:18:07.458
that I did, they were putting us up in an airbnb and I got stuck rooming

00:18:07.474 --> 00:18:09.282
with this guy that snored super loud.

00:18:09.346 --> 00:18:10.642
Like incredibly loud.

00:18:10.706 --> 00:18:13.206
You would not believe how loud it was if you heard it in person.

00:18:13.308 --> 00:18:14.866
So it was kind of hard to fall asleep.

00:18:14.898 --> 00:18:18.774
But just as I was finally falling asleep, I feel myself get bounced, like

00:18:18.812 --> 00:18:21.054
someone had jumped on the air mattress I was sleeping on.

00:18:21.092 --> 00:18:24.302
So immediately I wake up and I look around and there's nobody there.

00:18:24.356 --> 00:18:26.926
The guy's still snoring on the other side of the room and there was no one

00:18:26.948 --> 00:18:27.566
else around.

00:18:27.668 --> 00:18:30.206
I'm not a believer when it comes to ghosts, but I'd never been able to

00:18:30.228 --> 00:18:33.306
explain that one until I learned about waking dreams, which can include

00:18:33.338 --> 00:18:34.942
physical hallucinations as well.

00:18:34.996 --> 00:18:36.862
So I think that's what's happening to Nancy here.

00:18:36.916 --> 00:18:39.634
Her body is shutting down, and those hallucinations are starting to happen

00:18:39.672 --> 00:18:42.578
while she's still awake, allowing Freddy to affect her in the real world in

00:18:42.584 --> 00:18:43.282
a minor way.

00:18:43.336 --> 00:18:46.366
But meanwhile, across the street, Glen has fully fallen asleep.

00:18:46.398 --> 00:18:49.326
And just like Nancy was pulled underwater in the bath, Freddy pulls Glen

00:18:49.358 --> 00:18:50.710
down into a void in his bed.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:54.146
Moments before, a fountain of blood explodes from it, completely repainting

00:18:54.178 --> 00:18:55.238
the ceiling of his room.

00:18:55.324 --> 00:18:58.886
With all three of Nancy's friends now dead, Freddy uses them against her as

00:18:58.908 --> 00:19:02.086
she intentionally travels back into dreamland, hoping to bring Freddy out

00:19:02.108 --> 00:19:03.322
into the real world with her.

00:19:03.376 --> 00:19:06.326
As she travels down into the boiler room, she hears echoes of her dead

00:19:06.358 --> 00:19:09.340
friends calling to her and Freddy's laughter as he taunts her.

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:11.910
–[Freddy] I’m gonna get you!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.102
He stalks her from around corners as she goes deeper into the boiler room,

00:19:17.156 --> 00:19:19.694
eventually chasing her through dream space back to her house.

00:19:19.732 --> 00:19:23.054
But to his surprise, instead of running from him, she tackles him just

00:19:23.092 --> 00:19:26.250
before her alarm goes off and takes her back to the world of the awake.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:29.858
I don't want to get too picky here, because none of this is real, but I feel

00:19:29.864 --> 00:19:33.166
like if Freddy Krueger was real that this plan wouldn't work, because clocks

00:19:33.198 --> 00:19:34.814
never seem to work properly in a dream.

00:19:34.862 --> 00:19:37.522
And also you can have a dream that feels really long, but it was actually

00:19:37.576 --> 00:19:39.010
pretty short in real world time.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:42.178
They do an amazing job of conceptualizing this in the movie Inception.

00:19:42.274 --> 00:19:45.254
Anyway, Freddy is carried through back into the real world for the first

00:19:45.292 --> 00:19:48.502
time in 13 years, but that's not going to stop him from going after her.

00:19:48.556 --> 00:19:51.602
Only he finds that in this world, everything has been rigged with traps.

00:19:51.666 --> 00:19:54.678
He opens a locked door, only to be gut checked with a hammer, trips over a

00:19:54.684 --> 00:19:57.798
wire that sets off an exploding light bulb, and gets bombarded with a jug of

00:19:57.804 --> 00:20:00.010
kerosene to set the stage for a Freddy flavored barbecue.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.302
But this is nothing that he hasn't dealt with before.

00:20:02.356 --> 00:20:05.626
The now flaming Freddy stays hot on her heels, literally, but he's door

00:20:05.658 --> 00:20:06.922
checked back down the stairs.

00:20:06.986 --> 00:20:09.994
Still, he's somehow able to break out of the basement and sneak past Nancy

00:20:10.042 --> 00:20:13.386
up the stairs and into the room of Nancy's mother, Marge, one of the parents

00:20:13.418 --> 00:20:16.414
responsible for killing him the first time and stealing his glove.

