As he tries to stab her in the back, he disintegrates into a cosmic

00:21:04.058 --> 00:21:05.370
shadow and disappears.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.578
As I mentioned a lot, the rules tend to change a lot in this franchise, but

00:21:08.584 --> 00:21:11.246
there are a few other moments that are consistent with Freddy's defeat here.

00:21:11.278 --> 00:21:14.386
In A Nightmare on Elm Street 2, Nancy further explains how she

00:21:14.408 --> 00:21:16.738
eventually beat Freddy on the last page of her diary.

00:21:16.834 --> 00:21:18.360
-[Lisa] He is evil itself.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:22.086
-[Lisa] I know now that I brought him into my world.

00:21:22.188 --> 00:21:23.222
-[Lisa] We all did.

00:21:23.356 --> 00:21:25.590
-[Lisa] Gave him all the energy he needed.

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.594
-[Lisa] Our screams were all he needed.

00:21:28.732 --> 00:21:30.614
The concept is touched on again in Freddy vs. Jason,

00:21:30.662 --> 00:21:32.138
