00:22:50.056 --> 00:22:53.666
The now infamous 1428 Elm Street, and his son, Jesse Walsh, takes up

00:22:53.688 --> 00:22:55.042
residence in Nancy's old room.

00:22:55.096 --> 00:22:58.206
It doesn't take long for his dreams to go dark, including one where Freddy

00:22:58.238 --> 00:23:00.934
is a school bus driver who drives them into a giant fissure to hell.

00:23:00.972 --> 00:23:03.986
And one where he sees Freddy retrieving the finger blade glove from the boiler

00:23:04.018 --> 00:23:07.080
in the basement and asks for his help on some special work.

00:23:07.266 --> 00:23:11.303
-[Freddy] I need you Jesse. We’ve got special work to do here.

00:23:11.596 --> 00:23:12.454
-[Freddy] You and me.

00:23:12.572 --> 00:23:17.838
-[Freddy] You've got the body, I've got the brain.

00:23:18.034 --> 00:23:20.294
Necessary information, Jesse is gay.

00:23:20.342 --> 00:23:23.286
So Krueger's remarks here are once again playing into those psychosexual themes

00:23:23.318 --> 00:23:26.218
which I talk about more in my Things You Missed episode on Freddy's Revenge.

00:23:26.234 --> 00:23:29.578
But to quickly sum it up, the Jesse arc follows different rules

00:23:29.594 --> 00:23:30.378
than the Nancy arc.

00:23:30.394 --> 00:23:33.406
And this time, Freddy's goal is to take over Jesse's body and make him do

00:23:33.428 --> 00:23:36.254
the killing as a metaphor for the shame that Jesse feels by still being

00:23:36.292 --> 00:23:37.818
closeted about his sexuality.

00:23:37.914 --> 00:23:41.054
This comes out again the next night when Jesse has a dream where it's so hot

00:23:41.092 --> 00:23:42.634
that everything in his room is melting.

00:23:42.682 --> 00:23:45.398
So he goes to the basement, where he finds Freddy's glove hidden in the furnace,

00:23:45.404 --> 00:23:48.274
and Freddy encourages him to try putting it on and killing.

00:23:48.322 --> 00:23:51.426
The following evening, the Walsh's pet bird breaks out of its cage, flies

00:23:51.458 --> 00:23:54.114
around, attacks the family, then bursts into flame.

00:23:54.242 --> 00:23:55.890
-[Ken] There’s got to be a rational explanation.

00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:58.498
-[Ken] I mean, animals don’t just explode into flames for no reason.

00:23:58.674 --> 00:24:00.322
Excellent observation, Ken.

00:24:00.386 --> 00:24:03.226
The moment also represents the point where Freddy isn't just limited to

00:24:03.248 --> 00:24:03.990
dreams anymore.

00:24:04.070 --> 00:24:04.858
For some reason.

00:24:04.944 --> 00:24:06.554
His next move comes later that night.

00:24:06.592 --> 00:24:09.654
While Jesse's gym teacher is making him run laps as punishment for sneaking

00:24:09.702 --> 00:24:12.698
into a bar, Freddy brings all the gym equipment to life and uses it to

00:24:12.704 --> 00:24:15.694
attack the coach, eventually tying him up with a jump rope before taking

00:24:15.732 --> 00:24:18.910
control of Jesse's body and using it to slash Coach Schneider in the back.

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:22.398
When the fog clears, Jesse finds himself wearing the glove that he found the

00:24:22.404 --> 00:24:22.910
other night.

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:26.354
He screams when he realizes what he's done, which suggests that this time

00:24:26.392 --> 00:24:29.474
Freddy is using his powers to simulate another sleep phenomena, Somnambulism.

00:24:29.512 --> 00:24:32.030
More commonly known as sleepwalking.

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:35.362
But once again, it's not very realistic that Freddy would be able to control

00:24:35.416 --> 00:24:36.222
a sleepwalker.

00:24:36.286 --> 00:24:39.550
Sleepwalking occurs during non REM sleep, during which there are no dreams.

00:24:39.630 --> 00:24:42.306
So when someone sleepwalks, they aren't actually acting out their dreams.

00:24:42.338 --> 00:24:44.274
It's more of a misfired signal in the brain.

00:24:44.322 --> 00:24:47.346
But we have seen Freddy demonstrate an ability to toss around someone whose

00:24:47.378 --> 00:24:50.150
dream he's invading, like what happened with Tina and Glen, for example.

00:24:50.220 --> 00:24:53.686
So maybe he's just doing that in a more controlled way to manipulate Jesse

00:24:53.718 --> 00:24:55.066
into doing whatever he wants.

00:24:55.168 --> 00:24:56.810
More weird nightmares would follow.

00:24:56.880 --> 00:25:00.106
The next night, he found Freddy's glove moving on its own in the drawer and

00:25:00.128 --> 00:25:03.266
even dreamt of his own sister jump roping while singing the Freddy Krueger

00:25:03.318 --> 00:25:03.994
nursery rhyme.

00:25:04.042 --> 00:25:07.118
In the morning, their toaster catches fire, even though it's not plugged in.

00:25:07.204 --> 00:25:09.200
-[Ken] Craziest damn thing I've ever seen.

00:25:09.570 --> 00:25:13.578
Dad, what about the bird that exploded yesterday?

00:25:13.594 --> 00:25:16.162
In the evening, Freddy possesses Jesse's body again, and he visits his sister's room.

00:25:16.216 --> 00:25:19.060
But when he speaks out to her, Freddy's voice comes out.

00:25:19.060 --> 00:25:21.060
-[Freddy] Wake up, little girl.

00:25:21.350 --> 00:25:22.834
So then she does wake up.

00:25:22.872 --> 00:25:25.426
Clearly sees her brother standing there and asks what time it is.

00:25:25.448 --> 00:25:29.637
And when he tells her, it's in Jesse's voice again because she's no longer asleep.

00:25:29.637 --> 00:25:32.665
–[Jesse] It’s late, go back to sleep.

00:25:32.970 --> 00:25:35.926
So which one is it? You want her to wake up or go to sleep? Make up your mind.

00:25:35.948 --> 00:25:39.126
Now, up until this point, Freddy has kind of been able to fly under

00:25:39.148 --> 00:25:39.682
the radar.

00:25:39.746 --> 00:25:41.634
Some of his victims drew a big police presence.

00:25:41.682 --> 00:25:44.598
But because he only takes one victim at a time, and because all of his

00:25:44.604 --> 00:25:47.666
victims are asleep, there are only a couple witnesses who know that he's

00:25:47.698 --> 00:25:48.310
behind it.

00:25:48.380 --> 00:25:51.418
That would all change soon, because Lee Lisa Weber, a girl from Jesse's

00:25:51.434 --> 00:25:54.222
school who has a crush on him, holds a big pool party and, of course,

00:25:54.276 --> 00:25:55.114
invites Jesse.

00:25:55.162 --> 00:25:56.858
She tries to get it on with him in the cabana.

00:25:56.874 --> 00:26:00.382
But Freddy demonstrates his control by once again materializing a huge,

00:26:00.436 --> 00:26:01.870
rotting tongue in the real world.

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:05.322
For Jesse, this represents his true sexuality, which he's trying to hide.

00:26:05.386 --> 00:26:08.466
So when he realizes he's unable to control it, he gets out of there, which

00:26:08.488 --> 00:26:09.214
is actually smart.

00:26:09.262 --> 00:26:10.190
Good job, Jesse.

00:26:10.270 --> 00:26:13.874
Except he goes to visit the boy he most likely has an eye on Grady, which

00:26:13.912 --> 00:26:17.374
was not smart, because as he's there, he literally sees himself transform

00:26:17.422 --> 00:26:19.890
into Freddy, which is an agonizing process for him.

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:21.234
Jesse or Freddy.

00:26:21.282 --> 00:26:23.542
It's not really clear which one Grady can actually see.

00:26:23.596 --> 00:26:26.598
Puts on the finger blade, glove and gashes right through him as he bangs on

00:26:26.604 --> 00:26:27.446
the door for help.

00:26:27.548 --> 00:26:28.274
Rip. Grady.

00:26:28.322 --> 00:26:31.286
With the floodgates now open for Freddy to manipulate stuff in the real world, 

00:26:31.308 --> 00:26:34.838
he goes back to sabotage the pool party, locking everyone in, blowing

00:26:34.854 --> 00:26:37.930
up the lights, heating the pool to the point of boiling, and worst of all,

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.754
setting all the hot dogs on fire.

00:26:39.872 --> 00:26:43.462
Meanwhile, inside, Freddy takes over Jesse's body and attacks Lisa.

00:26:43.526 --> 00:26:47.786
He starts eating her leg for some reason, okay? But she gets away and tries

00:26:47.818 --> 00:26:50.282
to call out to Jesse, believing that he's still in there somewhere.

00:26:50.346 --> 00:26:53.118
She actually gets through to him, but it's clear that he's given up hope.

00:26:53.204 --> 00:26:54.530
-[Jesse] Kill me, Lisa.

00:26:55.270 --> 00:26:56.626
-[Jesse] Please kill me.

00:26:56.728 --> 00:27:00.146
And since Freddy's only real goal is to kill people and harvest souls, he

00:27:00.168 --> 00:27:01.570
just finds this amusing.

00:27:02.870 --> 00:27:05.860
♪ I heard a knock upon my door the other day ♪

00:27:06.550 --> 00:27:07.806
Natural reaction.

00:27:07.918 --> 00:27:09.246
Lisa stabs him in the shoulder.

00:27:09.278 --> 00:27:11.362
But even in the real world, that does no good.

00:27:11.416 --> 00:27:13.830
This is the same guy who used to cut himself all day for fun.

00:27:13.900 --> 00:27:16.742
He throws Lisa against the wall, but for now, he's gonna let her live.

00:27:16.796 --> 00:27:19.782
It's always hard for me to analyze his actions when they don't make any

00:27:19.836 --> 00:27:21.574
sense. But here goes.

00:27:21.692 --> 00:27:25.146
Freddy knew that Lisa loved Jesse, so he didn't see her as a threat and

00:27:25.168 --> 00:27:27.546
decided to go after the other guests at the pool party first.

00:27:27.648 --> 00:27:29.670
Everyone outside is confused by the commotion.

00:27:29.750 --> 00:27:31.180
Then this happens...

00:27:31.180 --> 00:27:32.658
–[Party Guest] What’s going on?

00:27:33.813 --> 00:27:36.905
(Freddy bursts through the deck)

00:27:37.170 --> 00:27:40.318
During this onslaught, nobody can escape because they're locked in and the

00:27:40.324 --> 00:27:41.310
fence is burning hot.

00:27:41.380 --> 00:27:44.746
Chaos ensues, the pool catches fire, and at least four teens are killed

00:27:44.778 --> 00:27:46.842
before Lisa's dad makes it outside with his gun.

00:27:46.906 --> 00:27:50.046
But knowing that Jesse is still in there somewhere, lisa actually prevents

00:27:50.078 --> 00:27:51.374
him from firing at Freddy.

00:27:51.422 --> 00:27:54.146
I guess the decision to keep her alive paid off for him, at least in the

00:27:54.168 --> 00:27:54.668
short term.

00:27:54.702 --> 00:27:57.666
Perhaps realizing the situation, though, like, that he could potentially get

00:27:57.688 --> 00:27:58.974
shot and die in the real world.

00:27:59.032 --> 00:28:02.322
He just walks to the edge of the party and bursts into flames.

00:28:02.466 --> 00:28:04.294
Nightmare 2 makes no sense. I tried, okay? 

00:28:04.412 --> 00:28:08.266
He goes back to his old base of operations, the boiler room

00:28:08.288 --> 00:28:12.010
at the now abandoned power plant, but soon finds that he's not alone.

00:28:12.010 --> 00:28:14.381
(IMPACT)

00:28:16.810 --> 00:28:20.204
♪ Mysterious Music ♪ 

00:28:20.590 --> 00:28:23.622
It isn't long before Freddy realizes he has a visitor.

00:28:23.686 --> 00:28:26.346
Lisa is still determined to get back her friend and crush Jesse.

00:28:26.378 --> 00:28:29.086
So Freddy stalks her from afar and tortures her with a series of

00:28:29.108 --> 00:28:32.538
hallucinations before aggressively appearing before her and nearly slicing

00:28:32.554 --> 00:28:33.326
her face open.

00:28:33.428 --> 00:28:35.182
-[Lisa] Jesse, I know you're in there.

00:28:35.316 --> 00:28:36.126
-[Lisa] Stop him.

00:28:36.228 --> 00:28:37.562
-[Freddy] No. Jesse's dead.

00:28:37.626 --> 00:28:40.846
He's about to finish her off when Lisa hears Jesse's voice and confesses

00:28:40.878 --> 00:28:41.634
her love for him.

00:28:41.672 --> 00:28:43.742
And this actually seems to physically hurt Freddy.

00:28:43.806 --> 00:28:46.622
For example, the spot that she stabbed him in earlier starts bleeding.

00:28:46.686 --> 00:28:49.446
And the more she says she loves him, the more pain he seems to be in.

00:28:49.468 --> 00:28:51.890
Lisa kisses him, and Freddy goes up in flame.

00:28:51.970 --> 00:28:54.642
His skin burns away, and he turns back into Jesse.

00:28:54.706 --> 00:28:58.086
Sticking with the sexuality metaphor, this is Jesse taking back hold of his

00:28:58.108 --> 00:28:59.394
ability to repress his feelings.

00:28:59.442 --> 00:29:01.270
He knows he'll hurt Lisa if he comes out.

00:29:01.340 --> 00:29:03.334
He knows people in his life will be ashamed of him.

00:29:03.372 --> 00:29:05.702
That's just the reality of the time period he lives in.

00:29:05.756 --> 00:29:07.126
So he's gotta get control of it.

00:29:07.148 --> 00:29:10.158
And in a literal sense, he gets control of Freddy, the hidden monster that

00:29:10.164 --> 00:29:11.498
is manipulating his actions.

00:29:11.594 --> 00:29:14.842
But like Nancy, five years before, the victory is only temporary.

00:29:14.906 --> 00:29:18.414
And before Jesse goes back to school, he dreams of another runaway bus where

00:29:18.452 --> 00:29:21.534
Freddy's hand bursts out of the classmate's chest and presumably makes good

00:29:21.572 --> 00:29:24.046
on his earlier promise and finishes him off.

00:29:24.148 --> 00:29:27.886
After 1986, the records of kids who died are not as well kept, because it

00:29:27.908 --> 00:29:30.494
seems like it's just become such a common thing that the school can't even

00:29:30.532 --> 00:29:31.262
keep up with it.

00:29:31.316 --> 00:29:34.898
We do find out about a kid in early 1987 who is most likely a Freddy victim. 

00:29:34.954 --> 00:29:37.910
-[Dr. Gordon] We lost a kid about a month ago to Fairview.

00:29:38.330 --> 00:29:41.574
-[Dr. Gordon] I don't know where he got the razors, but he cut off his own eyelids to stay awake.

00:29:41.612 --> 00:29:42.706
That's funny.

00:29:42.738 --> 00:29:45.078
I did the same thing when I was trying to make it through watching the

00:29:45.084 --> 00:29:46.498
Nightmare on Elm Street remake.

00:29:46.594 --> 00:29:49.446
At some point, Freddy finished taking out most all of the kids with

00:29:49.468 --> 00:29:52.758
connections to the group of parents who killed him in 1968, but there were a

00:29:52.764 --> 00:29:54.502
few leftovers who no longer lived there.

00:29:54.556 --> 00:29:57.378
These kids survived their first encounters with Freddy, but still incurred

00:29:57.394 --> 00:29:59.686
injuries during their nightmares, which made it look like they had each

00:29:59.708 --> 00:30:00.762
attempt did suicide.

00:30:00.826 --> 00:30:04.270
One example is Kristen Parker, most likely in spring 1987.

00:30:04.340 --> 00:30:07.518
Kristen dreamed that she was outside 1428 Elm Street and tried to save a

00:30:07.524 --> 00:30:08.686
little girl who wandered inside.

00:30:08.788 --> 00:30:11.678
As she tries to fend off Freddy in her dream, he manipulates things in the

00:30:11.684 --> 00:30:13.770
real world so that it looks like she slit her wrist.

00:30:13.850 --> 00:30:16.874
Her mom catches her and sends her to Westin Hills Psychiatric Hospital,

00:30:16.922 --> 00:30:19.666
where she joins several other kids who were deemed to be suicidal because of

00:30:19.688 --> 00:30:20.862
their encounters with Freddy.

00:30:20.926 --> 00:30:23.826
They were essentially held there against their will, but clearly, they were

00:30:23.848 --> 00:30:24.846
lucky to be alive.

00:30:24.958 --> 00:30:28.894
-[Reporter] And in local news, two more teenage deaths have occurred, both suicides.

00:30:29.022 --> 00:30:32.210
-[Reporter] County health officials are at a loss to explain this alarming trend.

00:30:32.290 --> 00:30:34.642
For Freddy, there are pros and cons to this strategy.

00:30:34.706 --> 00:30:37.926
On one hand, he can continue to consume more souls while covering up each

00:30:37.948 --> 00:30:40.694
death as something else, meaning his victims will be less informed and less

00:30:40.732 --> 00:30:41.622
prepared to fight him.

00:30:41.676 --> 00:30:44.726
The downside is that the public doesn't credit him with each kill, and the

00:30:44.748 --> 00:30:48.006
town's belief in him and fear of him is part of what gives him power, as we

00:30:48.028 --> 00:30:48.850
saw with Nancy.

00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:52.366
And speaking of Nancy, Freddy's greatest rival would resurface as a

00:30:52.388 --> 00:30:55.726
therapist at Western Hill, as a survivor, she's the only one who can help

00:30:55.748 --> 00:30:58.266
the kids who are captive there, because she's the only one who believes them.

00:30:58.298 --> 00:31:01.546
During Kristen's next nightmare, she's attacked by a giant worm

00:31:01.578 --> 00:31:04.202
incarnation of Freddy, and she pulls Nancy into her dream.

00:31:04.266 --> 00:31:07.038
Nancy finds a glass shard and stabs the creature in the eye, allowing

00:31:07.054 --> 00:31:07.922
Kristen to get free.

00:31:07.976 --> 00:31:11.700
When Freddy sees Nancy's face, he recognizes her as the one who got away.

00:31:11.700 --> 00:31:13.369
-[Freddy] You…

00:31:13.369 --> 00:31:15.614
Kristen was able to pull Nancy into her dream because of a unique ability

00:31:15.662 --> 00:31:18.574
she has, which would create a new challenge for the Springwood Slasher.

00:31:18.622 --> 00:31:21.558
Previously, he'd never really had to worry about his victims teaming up on him.

00:31:21.564 --> 00:31:24.658
The worst they could do was stand by to wake someone up if they sensed

00:31:24.674 --> 00:31:25.282
a nightmare.

00:31:25.346 --> 00:31:28.614
Kristen's ability made her especially dangerous, allowing the kids to fight

00:31:28.652 --> 00:31:29.190
back together.

00:31:29.260 --> 00:31:32.074
So Freddy got to work, taking out each of her friends in their own

00:31:32.112 --> 00:31:33.206
individual dreams.

00:31:33.318 --> 00:31:35.734
One patient, Philip, is an amateur puppeteer.

00:31:35.782 --> 00:31:38.906
So Freddy enters his dream and turns him into a human puppet, using his

00:31:38.928 --> 00:31:41.914
veins as strings, marching him to a third floor window and cutting him

00:31:41.952 --> 00:31:43.526
loose, causing him to fall to his death in both,

00:31:43.558 --> 00:31:46.894
the dream and the real world. Probably the most disturbing and

00:31:46.932 --> 00:31:48.846
creative kill in all of Freddy's history.

00:31:48.948 --> 00:31:52.446
The next night, he goes after Jennifer, an aspiring TV star, and pulls her

00:31:52.468 --> 00:31:54.080
head through the TV in her room.

00:31:54.080 --> 00:31:56.576
–[Freddy] Welcome to primetime b*tch!

00:31:58.130 --> 00:31:59.706
During a group hypnosis session, shortly after, 

00:31:59.738 --> 00:32:02.878
a mute patient named Joey wanders away from the group when he

00:32:02.884 --> 00:32:04.734
is distracted by a nurse that he has a crush on.

00:32:04.772 --> 00:32:06.742
Wait, Joey? She's a trap? Yeah.

00:32:06.796 --> 00:32:09.506
It turns out to be Freddy, who shoves his giant tongue down the kid's throat,

00:32:09.538 --> 00:32:12.838
then uses it to restrain him above the bed, which falls away into a

00:32:12.844 --> 00:32:13.750
giant pit of fire.

00:32:13.820 --> 00:32:15.094
It's always the tongue with this guy.

00:32:15.132 --> 00:32:18.018
I swear, I could do a whole video on just the history of Freddy Krueger's tongue.

00:32:18.034 --> 00:32:20.518
I'm getting flashbacks to the Grimace video at this point.

00:32:20.604 --> 00:32:23.162
It once again hints at the two themes that I keep coming back to.

00:32:23.216 --> 00:32:26.326
Freddy is implied to be a predator through his actions, and he's associated

00:32:26.358 --> 00:32:29.754
with the devil by suspending Joey over what is essentially a pit to hell.

00:32:29.872 --> 00:32:31.942
-[Ganon] No! Not into the pit!

00:32:32.006 --> 00:32:33.218
-[Ganon] It burns.

00:32:33.414 --> 00:32:36.154
Meanwhile, all the other patients are together in the group session,

00:32:36.202 --> 00:32:39.050
discovering how they can be whoever they want to in their dreams.

00:32:39.210 --> 00:32:44.400
-[Taryn In my dreams, I'm beautiful and bad.

00:32:44.930 --> 00:32:46.240
Uh, okay.

00:32:46.770 --> 00:32:47.870
Whatever you say.

00:32:47.940 --> 00:32:50.786
Freddy traps them using the same tactic he used at the pool party the

00:32:50.808 --> 00:32:51.362
previous year.

00:32:51.416 --> 00:32:54.178
When they try to escape, they realize the doorknobs are burning hot.

00:32:54.264 --> 00:32:57.186
Kind of an inconsistency, because in the first movie, touching something hot

00:32:57.208 --> 00:32:57.954
would wake you up.

00:32:57.992 --> 00:33:00.690
But maybe this is different because these kids are in a hypnosis.

00:33:00.770 --> 00:33:03.878
The room transforms into an industrial silo type thing, but luckily, a

00:33:03.884 --> 00:33:05.350
doctor discovers the sleeping group.

00:33:05.420 --> 00:33:08.566
However, because Joey was trapped by Krueger in the dream, he's unable to

00:33:08.588 --> 00:33:10.466
awaken, and he falls into a deep coma.

00:33:10.498 --> 00:33:13.474
It would be easy for him to just kill Joey at this point and take his soul,

00:33:13.522 --> 00:33:16.534
but Freddy wants revenge on Nancy for getting the best of him six years

00:33:16.572 --> 00:33:18.482
prior and uses Joey as a hostage.

00:33:18.546 --> 00:33:20.938
Kristen pulls everyone into the dream world to save him, but they're

00:33:20.954 --> 00:33:23.802
immediately ambushed and sent into their own little breakout dreams.

00:33:23.866 --> 00:33:26.766
Kristen dreams about her mother bringing home a guest who turns out to be

00:33:26.788 --> 00:33:29.994
Freddy in a bow tie, but she's able to use some parkour moves to escape.

00:33:30.042 --> 00:33:33.182
Taryn finds herself in an alley, where she notices some graffiti that says

00:33:33.236 --> 00:33:35.198
Taryn plus Freddy enclosed in a heart.

00:33:35.284 --> 00:33:39.006
Once again, Freddy is inappropriately tying himself to these kids in a

00:33:39.028 --> 00:33:40.186
romantic context.

00:33:40.298 --> 00:33:42.510
This would continue throughout the rest of Freddy's history.

00:33:42.580 --> 00:33:45.474
He takes the form of a pin up model, asks the girl if she wants to suck face,

00:33:45.522 --> 00:33:48.646
asks the girl if she wants to make babies, and even takes the form of

00:33:48.668 --> 00:33:49.330
another predator.

00:33:49.410 --> 00:33:50.546
Look, I'm not Chris Hansen.

00:33:50.578 --> 00:33:52.694
I'm not gonna point out every single time he does something like this.

00:33:52.732 --> 00:33:53.430
You get the idea.

00:33:53.500 --> 00:33:55.894
Freddy starts to use each kid's weaknesses against them.

00:33:55.932 --> 00:33:58.966
Taryn is a former addict, so Freddy transforms his finger blades into

00:33:58.988 --> 00:34:00.662
syringes, which he plunges into her.

00:34:00.716 --> 00:34:01.586
Will is disabled, in the real world. 

00:34:01.618 --> 00:34:04.666
He can only walk in his dream, so Freddy runs him down

00:34:04.688 --> 00:34:07.622
with what I can only describe as a giant BDSM wheelchair.

00:34:07.686 --> 00:34:10.486
He tries to conjure up some dream magic to destroy the chair and vanquish Freddy,

00:34:10.518 --> 00:34:12.540
but it's not enough to do anything.

00:34:12.540 --> 00:34:15.490
–[Freddy] Sorry kid. I don’t believe in fairy tales.

00:34:15.490 --> 00:34:17.594
It's cool to see Freddy evolving as a villain.

00:34:17.642 --> 00:34:20.426
In the beginning, he just terrorized Nancy and her friends with generic

00:34:20.458 --> 00:34:23.102
nightmare stuff, but now he's learned to tailor each nightmare towards

00:34:23.156 --> 00:34:24.110
whoever he's going after.

00:34:24.180 --> 00:34:27.326
The evolution fits nicely because it makes it all that more important for

00:34:27.348 --> 00:34:29.922
the remaining survivors to team up if they want to have a chance against him.

00:34:29.976 --> 00:34:32.926
They have strength in numbers because he can only tailor the nightmare

00:34:32.958 --> 00:34:33.890
to fit one person.

00:34:33.960 --> 00:34:37.686
But unfortunately for the group, there is only one person that he wants more

00:34:37.708 --> 00:34:41.560
than anyone, and their showdown would be six years in the making.

00:34:41.849 --> 00:34:44.634
(IMPACT)

00:34:46.288 --> 00:34:50.248
♪ Mysterious Music ♪ 

00:34:50.330 --> 00:34:53.578
The group finds Joey in the boiler room, which looks even more like an

00:34:53.584 --> 00:34:55.178
underworld realm than ever before.

00:34:55.264 --> 00:34:58.326
With their friends suspended over an even deeper hell pit, Freddy confronts Nancy,

00:34:58.358 --> 00:35:01.594
who foolishly demands that he let Joey go, and she has to run to save

00:35:01.632 --> 00:35:02.822
him from falling into the pit.

00:35:02.886 --> 00:35:05.678
This gives Krueger the perfect opportunity to push her in, but her new

00:35:05.684 --> 00:35:06.794
friends come to her rescue.

00:35:06.842 --> 00:35:09.354
Kristen knocks him back with a flying jump tackle.

00:35:09.482 --> 00:35:15.410
-[Seanthedeanzastudent] Okay, Angus is gonna knock down these chips using a flying jump tackle.

00:35:16.790 --> 00:35:19.262
Like I said, flying jump tackle.

00:35:19.326 --> 00:35:22.530
And Kincaid smashes him over the head with a giant metal pipe.

00:35:23.670 --> 00:35:27.186
I also like how Kincaid's dream power is just him being strong, even though

00:35:27.208 --> 00:35:28.034
he already is strong in the real world. 

00:35:28.072 --> 00:35:31.238
However, Krueger is able to stop him and lift him into the

00:35:31.244 --> 00:35:32.774
air with one arm while choking him.

00:35:32.812 --> 00:35:35.858
But their teamwork continues to be their advantage as Nancy finds a metal

00:35:35.874 --> 00:35:38.806
stake and thrusts it through Freddy's gut, which surprises him, but he

00:35:38.828 --> 00:35:40.342
simply laughs and pulls it out.

00:35:40.396 --> 00:35:43.722
Nancy comments on how he's never been this strong, and Freddy shows her why

00:35:43.776 --> 00:35:46.630
by revealing the screaming souls of the children that give him strength,

00:35:46.710 --> 00:35:49.738
meaning that with each victim he takes, he gets more and more powerful in

00:35:49.744 --> 00:35:50.458
the dream world.

00:35:50.544 --> 00:35:53.338
Keep that in mind, because it's gonna explain some anomalies later.

00:35:53.424 --> 00:35:56.554
But even with this additional power, he's not able to finish off Kincaid

00:35:56.602 --> 00:35:58.554
because he vanishes to go fight another battle.

00:35:58.602 --> 00:36:01.866
Apparently, he can only be in one place at a time, and he's got to go clash

00:36:01.898 --> 00:36:05.198
with one of the doctors from the hospital and Nancy's dad, who are together

00:36:05.284 --> 00:36:06.346
trying to bury his bones in the real world.

00:36:06.378 --> 00:36:09.506
They believe laying Freddy's bones to rest will end his curse.

00:36:09.528 --> 00:36:11.682
They're basically completely wrong about this.

00:36:11.736 --> 00:36:14.446
But for whatever reason, Freddy still wants to defend his bones.

00:36:14.478 --> 00:36:17.086
So he brings them to life and engages in combat as skelly Freddy.

00:36:17.118 --> 00:36:20.366
Maybe the reason for this is because it was his one chance to finally

00:36:20.408 --> 00:36:23.762
get back at Nancy's dad, one of the parents who lynched him 19 years prior.

00:36:23.826 --> 00:36:27.094
And he does just that, throwing Donald into a stake and impaling him.

00:36:27.132 --> 00:36:30.482
He also manages to knock out the doctor and does a little celebratory emote.

00:36:30.546 --> 00:36:32.902
I actually had to do a double take right here because I thought I was seeing

00:36:32.956 --> 00:36:35.880
actual footage of me whenever I have a video pop off.

00:36:37.930 --> 00:36:41.178
With that threat taken care of, Freddy returns to the dream world and freaks

00:36:41.194 --> 00:36:44.318
out the kids using a hall of mirrors, which very much needs to be a room if

00:36:44.324 --> 00:36:45.818
they ever do another Dream Warriors maze at Horror Nights.

00:36:45.834 --> 00:36:49.034
Each of them is pulled into a separate mirror, but Joey

00:36:49.082 --> 00:36:52.106
saves the day by screaming out for the first time and shattering the glass

00:36:52.138 --> 00:36:54.270
to save them, which seems to hurt Freddy as well.

00:36:54.340 --> 00:36:56.922
But he has one more trick up his striped sleeve.

00:36:56.986 --> 00:37:00.078
This time, he takes the form of Nancy's father, as if he's entering the

00:37:00.084 --> 00:37:02.190
dream world to tell her that he's crossed over.

00:37:02.260 --> 00:37:03.790
And this honestly doesn't make sense.

00:37:03.860 --> 00:37:06.694
You're not dreaming if you're dead, but it's enough to trick Nancy into

00:37:06.732 --> 00:37:07.622
letting her guard down.

00:37:07.676 --> 00:37:10.034
He turns back into Freddy and stabs her in the stomach.

00:37:10.082 --> 00:37:13.094
It looks like it may be over for the rest of the Dream Warriors as well.

00:37:13.132 --> 00:37:16.406
But with the last of her strength, Nancy jumps on his back and drives his

00:37:16.428 --> 00:37:18.162
own finger blades into his chest.

00:37:18.226 --> 00:37:21.270
And for the first time, Freddy is beaten on his home turf.

00:37:21.350 --> 00:37:24.794
But in the end, Nancy's sacrifice would basically go in vain, because

00:37:24.832 --> 00:37:27.878
there's still a light on at 1428 Elm Street.

00:37:27.974 --> 00:37:31.386
The survivors, Kristen. Kincaid and Joey, did get a little break from their

00:37:31.408 --> 00:37:34.202
striped sweatered saboteur, but when they went back to school that fall,

00:37:34.256 --> 00:37:36.078
Kristen began to see signs of his return.

00:37:36.164 --> 00:37:37.454
Yes, this is Kristen now.

00:37:37.492 --> 00:37:38.670
She got a makeover, okay.

00:37:38.740 --> 00:37:40.650
She also got a boyfriend named Rick.

00:37:40.730 --> 00:37:43.678
I personally wouldn't be rushing out to date the new girl fresh out of a

00:37:43.684 --> 00:37:46.238
psychiatric hospital, but Rick doesn't seem to mind.

00:37:46.324 --> 00:37:49.074
In fact, they are so in love that they apparently don't notice this huge,

00:37:49.112 --> 00:37:50.526
glowing slash in the lockers.

00:37:50.558 --> 00:37:52.386
More evidence of Freddy's imminent return.

00:37:52.488 --> 00:37:55.966
And that return would become a reality that evening when Kincaid has a dream

00:37:55.998 --> 00:37:58.882
about the auto salvage where Freddy's bones were buried earlier that year.

00:37:58.936 --> 00:38:02.166
He sees his dog prodding at the burial spot and goes to take a piss, but

00:38:02.188 --> 00:38:03.714
instead emits a stream of flame.

00:38:03.762 --> 00:38:07.046
And Kincaid watches as crevices in the earth open up to make way for

00:38:07.068 --> 00:38:08.134
Freddy's reassembly.

00:38:08.182 --> 00:38:11.450
His flesh rots in reverse until his true hellish form is

00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:12.410
completely restored.

00:38:12.410 --> 00:38:15.837
–[Freddy] You shouldn’t have buried me, I’m not dead.

00:38:16.190 --> 00:38:17.686
No, actually, he is dead.

00:38:17.718 --> 00:38:20.742
But as long as the dream demons still reside within him, he has the ability

00:38:20.806 --> 00:38:23.078
to come back and haunt more teenage dreams.

00:38:23.174 --> 00:38:26.046
So even when Kincaid pushes a car from above to crush him.

00:38:26.068 --> 00:38:29.614
He just responds again, and eventually, Kincaid's luck runs out, and he gets

00:38:29.652 --> 00:38:31.098
a gut full of finger blades.

00:38:31.194 --> 00:38:33.354
So at this point, there's not much for me to analyze.

00:38:33.402 --> 00:38:36.446
It's pretty obvious that no amount of killing Freddy in the dream world will

00:38:36.468 --> 00:38:39.338
ever do away with him, and it would be some time before anyone else figures

00:38:39.354 --> 00:38:40.990
out how to bring him out into the real world.

00:38:41.060 --> 00:38:43.918
His immediate goal is to finish off the Elm Street children that managed to

00:38:43.924 --> 00:38:46.102
escape him at Westin Hills.

00:38:46.156 --> 00:38:49.238
After Kincaid, that continues with Joey, who is once again tricked by Freddy

00:38:49.244 --> 00:38:52.498
taking the form of his crush, this time a pin up model from a poster

00:38:52.514 --> 00:38:53.554
before he's pulled down into his waterbed.

00:38:53.602 --> 00:38:55.762
Kind of similar to what happened to Nancy in the bathtub.

00:38:55.826 --> 00:38:58.786
Kristen tries to dream about a place that Freddy would never go and finds

00:38:58.818 --> 00:39:01.906
herself at the beach, but Freddy's glove emerges from the water like a shark

00:39:01.938 --> 00:39:03.082
fin, not even hitting land slows it down

00:39:03.136 --> 00:39:06.038
and with a blast, she finds her worst nightmare standing

00:39:06.054 --> 00:39:10.134
before her with some pretty stylish shades, but not as stylish as my YouTube specs.

00:39:10.182 --> 00:39:13.366
Alice's choice of venue ends up working against her when Freddy

00:39:13.398 --> 00:39:15.882
manipulates the dream, turning beach sand into quicksand.

00:39:15.946 --> 00:39:19.246
But as Kristen sinks down, she emerges in a decayed Elm Street house and

00:39:19.268 --> 00:39:20.830
soon finds herself in the boiler room.

00:39:20.900 --> 00:39:23.886
Fittingly, he was chasing her to the spot where he had ended the lives of so

00:39:23.908 --> 00:39:26.020
many of the neighborhood's kids before her.

00:39:26.020 --> 00:39:29.430
–[Freddy] Elm Street’s last brat. Farewell.

00:39:29.430 --> 00:39:32.174
And there's a good reason he allowed her to be the last survivor.

00:39:32.222 --> 00:39:35.086
He didn't want her to use her special ability to pull in any Dream Warrior

00:39:35.118 --> 00:39:38.398
reinforcements, as she had in the past, but due to her fear, she

00:39:38.424 --> 00:39:40.534
accidentally pulls someone into her dream anyway.

00:39:40.652 --> 00:39:44.210
This is Alice Johnson, Kristen's classmate and the sister of her boyfriend.

00:39:44.290 --> 00:39:47.366
Realizing her mistake, Kristen tries to shield the innocent Alice by

00:39:47.388 --> 00:39:50.278
attacking Freddy, but he effortlessly grabs her and hurls her into the

00:39:50.284 --> 00:39:53.926
raging furnace, certainly one of the most brutal ways to go since Freddy

00:39:53.958 --> 00:39:55.174
himself was burned to death.

00:39:55.222 --> 00:39:56.602
It's a moment of closure for him.

00:39:56.656 --> 00:39:59.658
The last links to the Elm Street families who killed him would go out the

00:39:59.664 --> 00:40:00.698
same way that he did.

00:40:00.784 --> 00:40:03.626
He proudly displays his collection of tortured souls in preparation for

00:40:03.648 --> 00:40:06.766
absorbing Kristen, but even in death, she proves to be difficult, and

00:40:06.788 --> 00:40:10.366
instead of being absorbed by him, she passes through his body to Alice in

00:40:10.388 --> 00:40:12.558
order to pass her dream powers on to her friend.

00:40:12.644 --> 00:40:16.190
Upon waking, Alice sees a new postcard on her mirror, Greetings From Hell!

00:40:16.260 --> 00:40:19.534
And as we've come to expect, Freddy is holding Kristen almost like a lover.

00:40:19.582 --> 00:40:22.418
Alice and Rick rush over to Kristen's house to find her room already in flames.

00:40:22.424 --> 00:40:24.882
It was too late to save her, so that was it.

00:40:24.936 --> 00:40:27.922
The Elm Street parents tried to get their revenge on Freddy, but in the end,

00:40:27.976 --> 00:40:31.074
he won, finishing off every last one of their descendants.

00:40:31.202 --> 00:40:34.406
But that didn't mean he was about to step away and quietly begin his retirement.

00:40:34.428 --> 00:40:36.662
And I can actually relate to this.

00:40:36.716 --> 00:40:39.494
When I first started getting serious about YouTube, my goal was to reach

00:40:39.532 --> 00:40:40.722
10,000 subscribers.

00:40:40.786 --> 00:40:44.282
But when I did that, that silver plaque started looking not so out of reach.

00:40:44.336 --> 00:40:46.342
So I went for 100,000 subscribers.

00:40:46.406 --> 00:40:50.186
And when I got that, the glint of gold caught my eye, and I thought for sure

00:40:50.208 --> 00:40:51.498
I'd chill out after a million.

00:40:51.584 --> 00:40:52.602
And at first, I did.

00:40:52.656 --> 00:40:55.662
But then I started to develop new goals, some of which you'll find out about

00:40:55.716 --> 00:40:56.718
in about a month.

00:40:56.804 --> 00:40:59.486
I think I've learned that if you have that drive to succeed, you're never

00:40:59.508 --> 00:41:00.682
going to be fully satisfied.

00:41:00.746 --> 00:41:02.778
And Freddy definitely has that drive.

00:41:02.884 --> 00:41:05.298
Maybe that's why the Dream Demons chose him.

00:41:05.384 --> 00:41:08.654
After eliminating the last of the Elm Street kids, he would broaden his hunt

00:41:08.702 --> 00:41:11.010
to the entire town of Springwood.

00:41:11.010 --> 00:41:13.010
(IMPACT)

00:41:16.322 --> 00:41:19.634
♪ Static Music ♪

00:41:19.910 --> 00:41:20.994
At Westin Hills, 

00:41:21.042 --> 00:41:24.166
Freddy used each of the kids' weaknesses against them, so as he turned his

00:41:24.188 --> 00:41:27.366
attention to the entire city, he decided to have some fun and toy with their

00:41:27.388 --> 00:41:28.262
fears as well.

00:41:28.316 --> 00:41:31.366
The first victim is Alice's asthmatic friend Sheila, who's worried about her

00:41:31.388 --> 00:41:33.218
astrology test when she dozes off.

00:41:33.244 --> 00:41:36.266
During it, Freddy sucks the oxygen out of her skull, causing her eyes to

00:41:36.288 --> 00:41:37.882
sink in and her skin to dry up.

00:41:37.936 --> 00:41:40.826
Rick is still struggling with grief over his girlfriend's death, and he

00:41:40.848 --> 00:41:43.578
apparently falls asleep on the toilet and sees Freddy use the form of

00:41:43.584 --> 00:41:46.190
Kristen to entice him before scaring the crap out of him.

00:41:46.260 --> 00:41:49.214
Pun actually not intended, believe it or not.

00:41:49.252 --> 00:41:52.346
The bathroom stall turns into an elevator ride down to a Japanese dojo,

00:41:52.378 --> 00:41:55.962
which for some reason, is decorated with an early prototype of the IGN logo.

00:41:56.026 --> 00:41:59.114
Rick's karate skills actually help him get the better of Freddy, but Krueger

00:41:59.162 --> 00:42:01.966
takes a cheap shot by launching his glove into his opponent before he can react.

00:42:01.988 --> 00:42:05.158
Alice's next dream features her getting sucked into the screen a

00:42:05.164 --> 00:42:07.190
movie theater, which lands her at her place of work.

00:42:07.260 --> 00:42:09.494
Her biggest fear is waiting tables her entire life.

00:42:09.532 --> 00:42:12.630
So Freddy shows her imagery of an older version of herself still working there.

00:42:12.700 --> 00:42:15.558
But when he appears at the counter next to her, he doesn't try to

00:42:15.564 --> 00:42:16.012
kill her.

00:42:16.012 --> 00:42:18.886
And there's a reason for it, which is demonstrated when the older version of

00:42:18.908 --> 00:42:22.098
Alice brings him a pizza topped with meatballs resembling the souls of his victims.

00:42:22.124 --> 00:42:25.386
Because of her uncontrolled new ability to pull others into her dreams,

00:42:25.408 --> 00:42:28.390
Alice is essentially serving her friends right up to Freddy.

00:42:28.470 --> 00:42:32.054
And next in line is her friend Deb, whose greatest fear became cockroaches

00:42:32.102 --> 00:42:34.110
after she found one in her food earlier that week.

00:42:34.180 --> 00:42:35.514
Nobody show her The Babadook. Okay? 

00:42:35.562 --> 00:42:38.986
During her workout session, she finds she has an unexpected spotter,

00:42:39.018 --> 00:42:41.322
who pushes her barbell down and snaps her elbows.

00:42:41.386 --> 00:42:44.746
Roach like appendages jut out from her broken arms, and she slowly turns

00:42:44.778 --> 00:42:48.094
into an insect and finds that she's a prisoner in a giant bug trap.

00:42:48.142 --> 00:42:50.926
It's a new twist on the commonly reported nightmare of running in slow

00:42:50.958 --> 00:42:53.182
motion which we saw before with Nancy and Kristen.

00:42:53.246 --> 00:42:56.606
Freddy watches through a small hole as she becomes her own worst nightmare

00:42:56.638 --> 00:42:58.830
then crushes her inside the roach motel.

00:42:58.910 --> 00:43:01.398
He also does something that we've never seen him do before.

00:43:01.484 --> 00:43:04.646
In order to prevent Alice and her love interest, Dan, from interfering he

00:43:04.668 --> 00:43:07.558
puts them in an infinite loop where they meet up at the diner then go to

00:43:07.564 --> 00:43:10.614
save Deb but just keep resetting back to the diner, where they have to start

00:43:10.652 --> 00:43:11.350
all over again.

00:43:11.420 --> 00:43:14.486
What they're experiencing is another representation of a real world sleep

00:43:14.518 --> 00:43:16.742
phenomena known as a false awakening loop.

00:43:16.806 --> 00:43:18.902
Most people have experienced this to some extent.

00:43:18.966 --> 00:43:21.482
You're dreaming, and then you wake up and start going through your morning routine.

00:43:21.536 --> 00:43:24.902
Then you actually wake up and realize it was all a dream.

00:43:24.966 --> 00:43:27.806
For most, this will only happen once but for others, it can happen, like,

00:43:27.828 --> 00:43:30.282
ten times hence the name false awakening loop.

00:43:30.346 --> 00:43:33.454
As with everything related to dreams, we only have theories about why this happens.

00:43:33.492 --> 00:43:35.530
No hard scientific conclusion.

00:43:35.610 --> 00:43:38.046
For normal people, it's often associated with anxiety, for an 

00:43:38.078 --> 00:43:41.858
important event, like a job interview or like Halloween, that's an

00:43:41.864 --> 00:43:42.530
important event.

00:43:42.600 --> 00:43:45.330
In Alice's case, she may be stressed out about saving her friend.

00:43:45.400 --> 00:43:48.946
Others have suggested that small noises or interruptions can interrupt your

00:43:48.968 --> 00:43:52.166
REM sleep without fully waking you up causing your dream to reset to

00:43:52.188 --> 00:43:52.882
something familiar.

00:43:52.946 --> 00:43:55.974
Another theory is the protoconsciousness theory which is basically the idea

00:43:56.012 --> 00:43:58.838
that your brain is trying to prepare you for the real world by showing you a

00:43:58.844 --> 00:44:00.370
dream similar to your reality.

00:44:00.450 --> 00:44:03.194
This obviously wouldn't apply to Alice because she's not the only one

00:44:03.232 --> 00:44:04.390
manipulating her dreams.

00:44:04.470 --> 00:44:07.526
There's evidence to suggest a link between false awakenings and lucid dreams.

00:44:07.558 --> 00:44:10.278
Lucid dreams are just when you're dreaming but you know that you're dreaming.

00:44:10.294 --> 00:44:13.306
So the false awakening could be your brain trying to trick you

00:44:13.328 --> 00:44:14.582
into thinking that you're not dreaming.

00:44:14.646 --> 00:44:17.162
This is much more likely what's going on with Alice and Dan.

00:44:17.226 --> 00:44:20.142
Each time the dream resets they don't realize that they're dreaming until

00:44:20.196 --> 00:44:22.974
several repetitions in when they finally figure it out.

00:44:23.012 --> 00:44:25.966
Again, I have to give credit to the movie Inception for conceptualizing this so well.

00:44:25.988 --> 00:44:29.298
The protagonist, Cobb is essentially a professional lucid dreamer,

00:44:29.304 --> 00:44:31.906
He uses totems to help him determine if he's dreaming or not.

00:44:32.008 --> 00:44:33.006
-[Cobb] This one was hers.

00:44:33.038 --> 00:44:34.206
-[Cobb] She'd spin it in the dream.

00:44:34.238 --> 00:44:35.330
-[Cobb] It would never talk.

00:44:35.480 --> 00:44:38.254
But there's a chilling concern that rises throughout the movie.

00:44:38.302 --> 00:44:41.510
That he may be getting lost in an infinite dream without realizing it.

00:44:41.580 --> 00:44:44.934
Personally, I find that idea more haunting than Freddy Krueger ever could be.

00:44:44.972 --> 00:44:47.746
But in Alice and Dan's case, they do escape from the dream

00:44:47.778 --> 00:44:50.626
When Freddy breaks the loop by appearing in the middle of the road.

00:44:50.658 --> 00:44:52.326
Alice tries to vehicular manslaughter him.

00:44:52.348 --> 00:44:53.446
But when she crashes into him.

00:44:53.468 --> 00:44:56.070
It's like hitting a bollard and the truck is crushed like a can.

00:44:56.140 --> 00:44:58.322
They wake up, realizing they've crashed into a tree.

00:44:58.386 --> 00:45:01.118
Dan is rushed to the hospital, where he's put under and has to deal with the

00:45:01.124 --> 00:45:02.794
dreams about Freddy Krueger as his surgeon.

00:45:02.842 --> 00:45:06.062
But Alice is okay and intentionally goes to sleep so she can try to enter

00:45:06.116 --> 00:45:07.262
his dream and save him.

00:45:07.316 --> 00:45:10.094
She's able to stall long enough for Dan to wake up, thus making him

00:45:10.132 --> 00:45:13.198
disappear from the dream to safety which should technically be the end of

00:45:13.204 --> 00:45:15.998
the dream because it was his dream to begin with, I think.

00:45:16.084 --> 00:45:19.006
But in light of the constantly changing rules in the Elm Street franchise,

00:45:19.038 --> 00:45:22.274
the nightmare continues and Alice finds herself in a church face to face

00:45:22.312 --> 00:45:23.486
with the devil himself.

00:45:23.598 --> 00:45:27.046
She fully realizes her title as the dream master by combining all of her

00:45:27.068 --> 00:45:28.434
friend's talents to fight Freddy.

00:45:28.482 --> 00:45:32.306
She uses Kristen's gymnastics, Rick's karate, Debbie's strength and Sheila's technology.

00:45:32.338 --> 00:45:36.390
But as we've seen before, Freddy can easily heal himself.

00:45:36.390 --> 00:45:41.210
–[Freddy] I. Am. Eternal.

00:45:41.210 --> 00:45:42.262
And this is true.

00:45:42.316 --> 00:45:45.174
It's very well established that you can't kill Freddy in the dream world.

00:45:45.212 --> 00:45:47.622
But what Alice does is essentially the next best thing.

00:45:47.676 --> 00:45:50.666
Using a broken shard of stained glass, she forces him to look his reflection

00:45:50.698 --> 00:45:53.694
and he sees all of the screaming souls of his victims trapped inside of him.

00:45:53.732 --> 00:45:55.102
This causes him immense pain.

00:45:55.156 --> 00:45:58.174
Alice hits him with a blast of light and an arm bursts out from within him

00:45:58.212 --> 00:46:00.970
as the souls of the dead attempt to climb their way out of his confines.

00:46:01.050 --> 00:46:04.158
The very souls that gave him power are now keeping him pinned down against a trellis.

00:46:04.164 --> 00:46:07.726
And finally his face bursts open allowing each of them to escape

00:46:07.758 --> 00:46:11.102
freely into the night, thanking Alice for finally ending their suffering.

00:46:11.166 --> 00:46:14.498
Although Freddy's skin, his sweater and his glove are left in to keep on

00:46:14.504 --> 00:46:17.478
the ground and things do go back to normal for a short while, it's only a

00:46:17.484 --> 00:46:20.038
matter of time before the nightmares would return.

00:46:20.204 --> 00:46:23.320
–[Kids] Nine, ten, he’s back again.

00:46:23.690 --> 00:46:27.942
Shortly before her high school graduation in June 1989, Alice would begin

00:46:27.996 --> 00:46:31.186
seeing visions in her dreams detailing the conception and birth of

00:46:31.218 --> 00:46:32.534
Frederick Krueger at the insane asylum.

00:46:32.582 --> 00:46:35.786
The last of these dreams shows him being reborn and growing up into his

00:46:35.808 --> 00:46:36.470
former glory.

00:46:36.550 --> 00:46:39.514
When she wakes up, there's one thing she's most confused about.

00:46:39.632 --> 00:46:40.710
-[Alice] It was Krueger.

00:46:40.870 --> 00:46:42.614
-[Alice] It happened while I was awake. Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:46:42.662 --> 00:46:45.646
How could Freddy be terrorizing her dreams,

00:46:45.668 --> 00:46:49.466
if she wasn't even asleep? This was a sly move by the

00:46:49.498 --> 00:46:50.442
Fedora Fatality Framer.

00:46:50.506 --> 00:46:52.858
Yes. I'm running out of ways to introduce this character.

00:46:52.954 --> 00:46:55.182
As you can see, we've been going for quite a while now.

00:46:55.236 --> 00:46:58.146
It was not her dreams that were playing host to Freddy, but rather the

00:46:58.168 --> 00:47:01.890
dreams of her unborn son who Freddy had found while hiding out inside her.

00:47:01.960 --> 00:47:04.494
She did not know it yet, but Dan had gotten her pregnant.

00:47:04.542 --> 00:47:07.678
And according to this one doctor later in the movie, an unborn fetus spends

00:47:07.694 --> 00:47:09.598
up to 70% of its time dreaming.

00:47:09.694 --> 00:47:13.254
Since it is literally my job to overthink everything, I did do that once again.

00:47:13.292 --> 00:47:16.214
I looked at a number of articles which all seem to agree that

00:47:16.252 --> 00:47:19.154
while we don't know for sure, it is likely that fetuses can dream.

00:47:19.202 --> 00:47:20.242
And I think that's believable.

00:47:20.306 --> 00:47:23.170
But my issue isn't about whether they can dream or not, it's the idea that

00:47:23.180 --> 00:47:25.450
they would be able to dream up scenes of the outside world.

00:47:25.520 --> 00:47:28.534
I imagine fetus dreams would be more of a series of sounds,

00:47:28.582 --> 00:47:30.282
temperature shifts and other sensory changes.

00:47:30.416 --> 00:47:33.594
However, we do know that Krueger has the ability to manipulate dreams, so

00:47:33.632 --> 00:47:36.750
maybe he's able to introduce a visual aspect, keep that in mind.

00:47:36.820 --> 00:47:40.046
But once again, this is all just theoretical, as with everything I've talked

00:47:40.068 --> 00:47:43.198
about in this video related to dream science because we have technology that

00:47:43.204 --> 00:47:46.270
can measure brain activity, but we don't have any tech that can record

00:47:46.340 --> 00:47:47.902
dreams as the dreamer sees them.

00:47:47.956 --> 00:47:50.734
And when it comes to remembering our dreams, our memories are very unreliable.

00:47:50.772 --> 00:47:53.886
Even if you remember your dream, you probably don't remember all

00:47:53.908 --> 00:47:54.212
of it.

00:47:54.212 --> 00:47:56.866
The hippocampus, the part of our brains that's responsible for storing memory,

00:47:56.898 --> 00:48:00.262
is not fully active during sleep and it takes some time to get going

00:48:00.316 --> 00:48:01.094
after you wake up.

00:48:01.132 --> 00:48:03.766
That's why it's so easy to forget about your dream if you don't write it

00:48:03.788 --> 00:48:04.438
down right away.

00:48:04.524 --> 00:48:07.682
That could be why nightmares are oftentimes more memorable than dreams.

00:48:07.746 --> 00:48:10.806
Nightmares simulate danger, causing our survival instincts to kick in and

00:48:10.828 --> 00:48:12.098
wake up the hippocampus.

00:48:12.194 --> 00:48:15.322
But going off memory is still pretty unreliable for those trying to study dreams.

00:48:15.376 --> 00:48:18.634
So until there's a way to record dreams, we'll likely never know

00:48:18.672 --> 00:48:20.230
what a fetus sees while it's dreaming.

00:48:20.310 --> 00:48:23.566
Which for now is good news if you're Freddy Krueger, who would continue his

00:48:23.588 --> 00:48:26.110
spree with a set of new victims.

00:48:26.110 --> 00:48:29.268
(IMPACT)

00:48:30.756 --> 00:48:34.740
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:48:34.930 --> 00:48:38.834
Despite losing some of his power a couple years earlier, Freddy is still well

00:48:38.872 --> 00:48:42.350
equipped to dish out chaos in the dreams of Springwood's teenage population.

00:48:42.430 --> 00:48:45.726
He finally gets to Dan, who's pulled into a dream while driving and crashes

00:48:45.758 --> 00:48:46.258
his car.

00:48:46.344 --> 00:48:49.546
Although he survives, he has the bright idea of switching to a motorcycle

00:48:49.598 --> 00:48:52.678
which is hijacked by a very terminator looking Freddy and sent out of

00:48:52.684 --> 00:48:54.210
control into oncoming traffic.

00:48:54.290 --> 00:48:56.662
Next he goes for members of Alice's new friend group.

00:48:56.716 --> 00:48:59.494
Greta is a student whose mother is pushing her to become a model, often

00:48:59.532 --> 00:49:00.850
criticizing her for her diet.

00:49:00.930 --> 00:49:03.846
Freddy pulls her into a dream during a dinner party and force feeds her to

00:49:03.868 --> 00:49:05.058
the point of asphyxiation.

00:49:05.154 --> 00:49:08.786
Mark is a comic book artist who is suddenly possessed to draw 1428 Elm Street. 

00:49:08.818 --> 00:49:11.786
He is pulled into his own drawing and nearly sucked into the birth

00:49:11.818 --> 00:49:12.986
canal where Freddy is hiding.

00:49:13.018 --> 00:49:14.734
But Alice gets there in time to save him.

00:49:14.772 --> 00:49:17.966
Yvonne, a member of the diving team, also has a close call at practice when

00:49:17.988 --> 00:49:20.926
the diving board below her breaks apart and the pool transforms into this

00:49:20.948 --> 00:49:24.042
puddle that transports her to what appears to be the inside of the boiler.

00:49:24.106 --> 00:49:25.226
She's seized by Freddy,

00:49:25.258 --> 00:49:29.054
But Alice once again comes to the rescue, impaling Freddy through the mouth

00:49:29.102 --> 00:49:30.578
with the wrong end of a pool net.

00:49:30.664 --> 00:49:34.014
All the while, Alice experiences several dreams featuring a young boy named Jacob,

00:49:34.062 --> 00:49:37.246
who she eventually comes to realize is a representation of her unborn

00:49:37.278 --> 00:49:40.466
son when she's pulled into a dream inside her own womb during an ultrasound

00:49:40.498 --> 00:49:43.442
and sees Freddy feeding the souls that he's collected to the baby.

00:49:43.506 --> 00:49:47.798
He's taking their souls, their spirit, and making the baby like him.

00:49:47.884 --> 00:49:50.838
I know we should probably be past the point of questioning when the rules of

00:49:50.844 --> 00:49:54.198
the Elm Street universe change, but seriously, does the baby dream about the

00:49:54.204 --> 00:49:56.710
real world or does the baby dream about the womb? Just pick one.

00:49:56.780 --> 00:49:59.778
The next victim is Mark, who is just kicking back and reading some comic books,

00:49:59.794 --> 00:50:02.766
but discovers that Freddy has taken over the pages with scenes of his

00:50:02.788 --> 00:50:03.898
friends being attacked.

00:50:03.994 --> 00:50:06.042
Once again, he's pulled into the world of the comic.

00:50:06.106 --> 00:50:08.986
He takes a page from the Dream Warriors by demonstrating a unique dream ability,

00:50:09.018 --> 00:50:11.818
 and turns himself into one of his super powered characters.

00:50:11.914 --> 00:50:14.894
But Freddy does the same, emerging in this comic book villain looking

00:50:14.932 --> 00:50:17.402
costume and referring to himself as Super Freddy.

00:50:17.466 --> 00:50:20.306
I guess we can give this one points for creativity, but it really feels like

00:50:20.328 --> 00:50:23.746
Freddy, and by extension, the creators of these movies, kind of forgot to

00:50:23.768 --> 00:50:25.122
try to be scary at some point.

00:50:25.176 --> 00:50:27.934
And it certainly doesn't help when Mark loses his three dimensional volume

00:50:27.982 --> 00:50:30.166
and Freddy simply shreds him into scrap paper.

00:50:30.268 --> 00:50:33.654
However, I am still highly anticipating Paper Freddy and The Thousand Year Door.

00:50:33.692 --> 00:50:36.306
With Yvonne and Alice as the two remaining survivors.

00:50:36.338 --> 00:50:39.606
Yvonne goes to look for the lost remains of Amanda Krueger, while Alice goes

00:50:39.628 --> 00:50:40.866
to sleep to confront Freddy Before he can do any more damage to her baby.

00:50:40.898 --> 00:50:43.738
She finds herself in the corridors of the asylum

00:50:43.744 --> 00:50:46.954
where she's chased but manages to lose him, then

00:50:46.992 --> 00:50:50.490
comes out of nowhere and rams him with his giant spiked baby stroller.

00:50:50.490 --> 00:50:55.218
(SCREAMS)

00:50:55.470 --> 00:50:58.426
I don't know why you would think a baby stroller with these giant metal spikes,

00:50:58.458 --> 00:51:01.226
but if I was a baby, this would definitely be my stroller.

00:51:01.258 --> 00:51:02.042
It's so metal.

00:51:02.106 --> 00:51:05.306
Freddy is tossed down a staircase into the ward for the criminally insane,

00:51:05.338 --> 00:51:07.434
and the inmates tear him apart limb from limb.

00:51:07.482 --> 00:51:10.686
But none of this seems to even be real, and he appears in another realm,

00:51:10.718 --> 00:51:14.194
which is basically an amalgamation of the church, the asylum, the diner and

00:51:14.232 --> 00:51:17.886
1428 Elm Street, all jumbled together in a twisted mess of MC Escher physics. 

00:51:17.918 --> 00:51:20.654
Here, Freddy can be seen trying to befriend Jacob.

00:51:20.702 --> 00:51:23.638
He most likely wants to keep Jacob alive and use him the same way that he

00:51:23.644 --> 00:51:26.918
tried to use Alice by having him pull others into his dreams to serve up to Freddy. 

00:51:26.924 --> 00:51:30.626
But when Jacob sees his mom, he realizes something is wrong and runs

00:51:30.658 --> 00:51:31.158
for it.

00:51:31.180 --> 00:51:34.410
Once he explains that Freddy is hiding out inside her, Alice is basically

00:51:34.480 --> 00:51:35.930
able to expel him from her body.

00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:39.226
And once Yvonne brings Amanda Krueger's ghost to the scene of the fight, she has some guiding words for Jacob.

00:51:39.248 --> 00:51:43.550
-[Amanda] Jacob! Alice will not triumph.

00:51:44.770 --> 00:51:46.766
-[Amanda] Only you can help her now.

00:51:46.868 --> 00:51:50.014
And he does that by basically turning into a mini Krueger and pretending to

00:51:50.052 --> 00:51:52.830
want to learn from Freddy and take his side, I guess.

00:51:52.900 --> 00:51:55.502
And then, using the power of the souls that Freddy had been feeding him,

00:51:55.556 --> 00:51:58.782
screams and hits him with a blast, pulling the baby Freddy out of his body

00:51:58.836 --> 00:52:01.950
as if it had just been piloting this Freddy Krueger mech suit the entire time.

00:52:02.020 --> 00:52:04.978
I guess that explains why he was looking so disjointed all summer then.

00:52:05.034 --> 00:52:08.806
In the aftermath, we see Alice's love for her child as she absorbs him

00:52:08.828 --> 00:52:12.114
back into her body, in contrast with Amanda, who only shows embarrassment

00:52:12.162 --> 00:52:14.230
towards her kid as she tries to absorb him.

00:52:14.300 --> 00:52:17.702
She warns Alice to just take her baby and leave, and it's not long before

00:52:17.756 --> 00:52:19.750
Freddy's arm slashes out from within her.

00:52:19.820 --> 00:52:23.226
The last thing we see is Amanda screaming in distress, unable to contain the

00:52:23.248 --> 00:52:24.422
evil that she had created.

00:52:24.486 --> 00:52:27.834
We never find out if Alice and Jacob managed to escape Springwood or

00:52:27.872 --> 00:52:31.034
Freddy's wrath, but we do know that over the next twelve years he came back.

00:52:31.072 --> 00:52:33.622
And this time he was totally uncontested.

00:52:33.686 --> 00:52:37.038
Taking out large swaths of teenagers as well as kids as young as six or

00:52:37.044 --> 00:52:37.838
seven years old.

00:52:37.924 --> 00:52:41.166
Some of them turned up in strange places, like the side of a highway, while

00:52:41.188 --> 00:52:43.422
others just seemed to go missing.

00:52:43.476 --> 00:52:46.838
One by one, Freddy did what he had never been able to do before

00:52:46.874 --> 00:52:48.478
with no Nancy Thompson, Kristen Parker or Alice Johnson.

00:52:48.494 --> 00:52:49.074
To stop him.

00:52:49.112 --> 00:52:52.674
He took out the entire population of kids and teenagers in Springwood, with

00:52:52.712 --> 00:52:54.302
just one kid who managed to escape.

00:52:54.366 --> 00:52:57.474
The remaining adults in town experienced some kind of mass psychosis,

00:52:57.522 --> 00:53:01.046
continuing to operate carnivals, schools and other experiences designed for kids,

00:53:01.068 --> 00:53:04.406
while seeming not to notice, or at least not to acknowledge that there

00:53:04.428 --> 00:53:05.560
are no kids anyway.

00:53:06.170 --> 00:53:12.150
-[Childless Woman] Oh, what beautiful, adorable children would you like to come and live with?

00:53:12.300 --> 00:53:14.554
Uh we should burn her alive next.

00:53:14.672 --> 00:53:18.102
As I mentioned, there was one survivor, and his name was John Doe.

00:53:18.166 --> 00:53:20.470
What's in the box? No, not that John Doe.

00:53:20.550 --> 00:53:21.994
No, it's not a placeholder name.

00:53:22.032 --> 00:53:23.386
His parents just hate him.

00:53:23.408 --> 00:53:27.742
Then again, my parents love me, yet they still named me Zack Morris in the 90s.

00:53:27.796 --> 00:53:31.246
And speaking of the 90s, A Nightmare on Elm Street, skips over them.

00:53:31.268 --> 00:53:32.746
At the beginning of Freddy's Dead: The Final Nightmare.

00:53:32.778 --> 00:53:35.102
A title says the events take place ten years from now.

00:53:35.156 --> 00:53:38.446
The movie came out in 1991, meaning that Freddy's next activity would be

00:53:38.468 --> 00:53:39.582
set in 2001.

00:53:39.636 --> 00:53:43.662
This discarded newspaper says April 22 on it, so let's call it April 2001.

00:53:43.716 --> 00:53:46.646
I guess Freddy was trying to tie up loose ends by killing John so he could

00:53:46.668 --> 00:53:48.914
enjoy Shrek and Weezer's Green album in peace the following month.

00:53:48.962 --> 00:53:52.246
John is taken on a wild dream where he's sucked out of an airplane,

00:53:52.268 --> 00:53:55.638
experiences a false awakening and sees Freddy dressed up as a

00:53:55.644 --> 00:53:58.802
wizard of Oz witch zooming around his house, which is in free fall.

00:53:58.866 --> 00:54:01.462
I guess Freddy's having some fun with this one to celebrate his last

00:54:01.516 --> 00:54:05.786
Springwood victim, the house lands at 1427 Elm Street.

00:54:05.808 --> 00:54:08.422
The very spot where Krueger took the life of Glen Lance 20 years beforehand.

00:54:08.486 --> 00:54:11.814
But John survives and hightails out to a Greyhound station where Krueger

00:54:11.862 --> 00:54:15.658
strikes him with a bus, which he also survives. John is break yeeted through a

00:54:15.664 --> 00:54:19.466
tear in reality back into the waking world, which has literally never been a

00:54:19.488 --> 00:54:20.262
thing before.

00:54:20.416 --> 00:54:24.240
When Freddy touches this portal, it closes on him and he says this...

00:54:24.240 --> 00:54:29.270
–[Freddy] Now be a good little doggy and go fetch.

00:54:29.270 --> 00:54:32.626
Like Alice and Jacob before him, John is being kept alive as part of

00:54:32.648 --> 00:54:33.378
Freddy's plan.

00:54:33.464 --> 00:54:36.606
This time he's trying to use him to get to his own biological daughter

00:54:36.638 --> 00:54:39.550
Katherine, who is now in her 40s and working as a psychiatrist in a

00:54:39.560 --> 00:54:41.490
shelter for troubled kids in a neighboring town.

00:54:41.570 --> 00:54:45.554
Why he needs John to do this is completely unclear since he is very capable

00:54:45.602 --> 00:54:49.222
of leaving the boundaries of Springwood but that is the explanation he gives

00:54:49.356 --> 00:54:55.526
-[John ] But you let me live!
–[Freddy] Only long enough for you to bring me back my daughter.

00:54:55.638 --> 00:54:58.698
Regardless, as John and Katherine drive back into town to find answers to

00:54:58.704 --> 00:55:01.710
the mysteries of their past, three other kids from the shelter stow away

00:55:01.780 --> 00:55:03.450
Carlos, Tracy and Spencer.

00:55:03.530 --> 00:55:06.798
Although these three are not from Springwood, that would not save them from

00:55:06.804 --> 00:55:08.510
the wrath of Freddy Krueger.

00:55:08.510 --> 00:55:11.750
(IMPACT)

00:55:13.817 --> 00:55:17.223
♪ Mysterious Music ♪ 

00:55:17.410 --> 00:55:21.726
The three runaways end up spending the night at 1428 Elm Street even though

00:55:21.748 --> 00:55:24.686
it looks totally different now, where Carlos is the next one to learn why

00:55:24.708 --> 00:55:26.146
there aren't any kids in Springwood.

00:55:26.178 --> 00:55:29.314
He dreams that Tracy is calling his name and turns a corner to find himself

00:55:29.362 --> 00:55:32.402
in some kind of flop house where his mom threatens to clean out his ears

00:55:32.466 --> 00:55:35.138
which may or may not be related to the reason that Carlos wears a hearing aid.

00:55:35.154 --> 00:55:38.466
The mom reveals herself to be none other than Freddy and sticks a giant

00:55:38.498 --> 00:55:39.878
cotton swab through his head.

00:55:39.964 --> 00:55:43.026
Somehow this doesn't kill him, so Freddy then throws him through a brick wall

00:55:43.058 --> 00:55:45.402
or at least some wallpaper of a brick wall.

00:55:45.456 --> 00:55:48.730
How hard would it have been to just make some foam bricks? I don't know.

00:55:48.800 --> 00:55:52.266
All I know is that Carlos ends up in the boiler room where Freddy taunts him

00:55:52.288 --> 00:55:54.182
for not being able to hear without his hearing aid.

00:55:54.246 --> 00:55:57.342
During this era, Freddy seems to spend less time killing and more time

00:55:57.396 --> 00:55:58.554
having fun with his victims.

00:55:58.602 --> 00:56:01.594
We don't know when his last kill was, but maybe he's just enjoying torturing

00:56:01.642 --> 00:56:03.938
this group because he hasn't had a victim in so long.

00:56:04.024 --> 00:56:06.354
Also, provided that he's been collecting souls this whole time.

00:56:06.392 --> 00:56:09.746
We can assume that he's extremely powerful now, so messing around would

00:56:09.768 --> 00:56:12.130
literally only serve for entertainment purposes.

00:56:12.130 --> 00:56:16.401
-[Carlos] Give me my hearing back!

00:56:16.710 --> 00:56:18.338
So Freddy does just that.

00:56:18.424 --> 00:56:21.382
But just like the time he complied with Nancy's request to let her friend go,

00:56:21.436 --> 00:56:24.290
his compliance comes with unintended side effects.

00:56:24.370 --> 00:56:27.746
Carlos' hearing aid turns into this little parasitic creature and amplifies

00:56:27.778 --> 00:56:30.886
the sound way too much to the point that dropping a pin would drive him insane.

00:56:30.908 --> 00:56:34.614
Then he threatens to drop a handful of pins, and Carlos screams,

00:56:34.662 --> 00:56:38.586
begging him to stop, which makes no sense because of the simple fact that

00:56:38.608 --> 00:56:40.054
you can hear your own voice.

00:56:40.102 --> 00:56:42.310
And this would be way louder than the pins dropping.

00:56:42.390 --> 00:56:43.838
Look, it's been a long video.

00:56:43.924 --> 00:56:46.330
My explanation is that this is just dream logic.

00:56:46.410 --> 00:56:49.166
After this, Freddy gives him the old nails on the chalkboard routine, and

00:56:49.188 --> 00:56:50.670
his head explodes.

00:56:53.810 --> 00:56:57.038
Meanwhile, Spencer, the stoner character of the group, falls asleep on the

00:56:57.044 --> 00:56:59.390
couch and sees this anti drug PSA on TV.

00:56:59.470 --> 00:57:02.626
But Freddy knocks out the host with a frying pan and hypnotizes Spencer into

00:57:02.648 --> 00:57:04.018
a psychedelic music video.

00:57:04.104 --> 00:57:07.198
We've seen Freddy use a similar tactic before, with Alice getting sucked

00:57:07.214 --> 00:57:09.202
into a movie and Mark into a comic book.

00:57:09.256 --> 00:57:12.386
I know I've had dreams where I start off watching a show, but then gradually

00:57:12.418 --> 00:57:14.230
find that I'm a character in that show.

00:57:14.300 --> 00:57:16.822
But strangely, when I tried looking this up to see if it was a common

00:57:16.876 --> 00:57:19.382
phenomenon, I couldn't find anyone who shared my experience.

00:57:19.516 --> 00:57:22.374
The closest thing I found was people reporting about fictional characters

00:57:22.422 --> 00:57:25.366
entering their world, but nothing about the dreamer entering the fictional world.

00:57:25.398 --> 00:57:31.006
In Spencer's case, he ends up inside of a video game.

00:57:31.108 --> 00:57:31.962
-[Ronnie]  ♪ My life is like a video game. ♪
Thank you, Ronnie.

00:57:32.026 --> 00:57:34.926
As he's manipulated by Freddy in the game world, his body mimics those

00:57:34.948 --> 00:57:37.966
movements in the real world, leading to him being air yeeted

00:57:37.988 --> 00:57:38.670
through a painting.

00:57:42.210 --> 00:57:43.866
-[John] I found Spencer.

00:57:43.978 --> 00:57:44.670
Oh, my God. Spencer, are you okay? 

00:57:44.740 --> 00:57:48.926
Do you need to go to the hospital?

00:57:48.958 --> 00:57:52.130
Freddy repeatedly stomps on him in the game, then makes him go

00:57:52.200 --> 00:57:53.090
full cartoon and basically destroys the house.

00:57:53.160 --> 00:57:55.938
At this point, John and Katherine have shown up, and John wants to enter the

00:57:55.944 --> 00:57:57.202
dream world to try to save him.

00:57:57.256 --> 00:58:00.150
There are so many problems with this, so let's talk about them.

00:58:00.220 --> 00:58:01.814
One, John doesn't really even know Spencer.

00:58:01.852 --> 00:58:04.806
Two, the reason that characters have been able to enter other

00:58:04.828 --> 00:58:07.766
characters' dreams before is because of the special ability passed from

00:58:07.788 --> 00:58:09.250
Kristen to Alice to Jacob.

00:58:09.330 --> 00:58:11.170
Nobody here is shown to have that ability.

00:58:11.250 --> 00:58:13.414
They shouldn't even be able to get into Spencer's dream.

00:58:13.462 --> 00:58:17.110
Three, John enters the dream world by asking Tracy to knock him unconscious.

00:58:17.190 --> 00:58:19.494
Being unconscious is not the same as being asleep.

00:58:19.542 --> 00:58:21.014
You aren't dreaming when you're unconscious.

00:58:21.062 --> 00:58:22.442
Your brain is basically shut down.

00:58:22.496 --> 00:58:25.726
But ignoring all of that, they discover Freddy enjoying his video game like

00:58:25.748 --> 00:58:27.550
a delighted eight year old on Christmas morning.

00:58:27.620 --> 00:58:29.450
So Tracy unplugs his controller.

00:58:29.530 --> 00:58:32.698
This does very little, though, because in this dream, Freddy's glove doubles

00:58:32.714 --> 00:58:35.214
as a Power glove, which, if you don't know what that is, it was a special

00:58:35.252 --> 00:58:38.778
controller used for the Nintendo Entertainment System in 1989 that allowed

00:58:38.794 --> 00:58:40.618
you to control certain games with hand movements.

00:58:40.714 --> 00:58:43.898
Freddy uses it to shut Tracy and John out and take control of Spencer's body,

00:58:43.914 --> 00:58:46.482
tossing him down the airs and into a bottomless pit.

00:58:46.546 --> 00:58:49.666
Katherine tries to gather Tracy and John and get the hell out of Springwood.

00:58:49.698 --> 00:58:52.566
But as John is still asleep in the back of the van, he dreams that he is in

00:58:52.588 --> 00:58:53.622
free fall once more.

00:58:53.676 --> 00:58:55.570
But Freddy has stowed away in his parachute.

00:58:55.650 --> 00:58:58.706
He reveals that Katherine is his daughter and that he only kept John alive

00:58:58.738 --> 00:58:59.382
to get to her.

00:58:59.436 --> 00:59:02.930
So he cuts him down from the parachute and also comically wheels in a bed of

00:59:02.940 --> 00:59:05.942
spikes for him to land on, because I guess just going splat on the ground

00:59:06.006 --> 00:59:07.226
wouldn't have been painful enough.

00:59:07.328 --> 00:59:10.666
Freddy absorbs his soul, and back at the shelter, nobody remembers the three

00:59:10.688 --> 00:59:14.014
boys ever existing, other than Doc, a therapist who works there and

00:59:14.052 --> 00:59:15.562
specializes in dream therapy.

00:59:15.626 --> 00:59:20.302
-[Doc] He didn't just kill Carlos and the others, he erased them.

00:59:20.356 --> 00:59:23.818
I mean, he's never done that before, but sure, add it to the list of rules

00:59:23.834 --> 00:59:24.614
that have changed.

00:59:24.682 --> 00:59:28.194
Katherine and Tracy are each tormented with dreams of an abusive father, but survive.

00:59:28.232 --> 00:59:31.374
In Tracy's case, she tries to fight back with martial arts,

00:59:31.422 --> 00:59:34.015
prompting Freddy to say this...

00:59:34.015 --> 00:59:37.917
–[Freddy] Kung fu this, b*tch!

00:59:43.940 --> 00:59:45.600
Sorry, I just need a minute.

00:59:48.580 --> 00:59:53.728
All right, who wrote this line? Michael De Luca.

00:59:53.824 --> 00:59:58.052
So after that lady from the carnival, my proposal is that we burn him next.

00:59:58.186 --> 00:59:59.620
Alright, I gotta get through this.

00:59:59.690 --> 01:00:02.712
So Doc has his own encounter with Freddy and fights him off with a bat,

01:00:02.766 --> 01:00:04.744
which is laughable for him at this point.

01:00:04.942 --> 01:00:09.160
-[Freddy] In dreams, I am forever.

01:00:10.860 --> 01:00:12.408
-[Freddy] Too bad you're not.

01:00:12.494 --> 01:00:15.736
Which has the exact same energy as one of the best lines in screenwriting

01:00:15.768 --> 01:00:17.016
history from Mortal Kombat: Annihilation

01:00:18.495 --> 01:00:21.062
–[Kitana] Mother! You’re alive.

01:00:21.558 --> 01:00:24.467
–[Sindel] Too bad you… will die!

01:00:24.708 --> 01:00:27.240
Anyway, the Freddy… (laughs) the Freddy.

01:00:27.320 --> 01:00:27.996
I'm losing it.

01:00:28.018 --> 01:00:29.164
Krueger's making me lose it.

01:00:29.202 --> 01:00:32.496
The doctor manages to rip off a piece of Freddy's sweater right before his

01:00:32.518 --> 01:00:35.696
alarm goes off and realizes that he brought the fabric out of the dream with him.

01:00:35.718 --> 01:00:39.196
This is really important because it gives him the idea to bring Freddy

01:00:39.228 --> 01:00:42.476
back out into the real world where he may be mortal, something that nobody

01:00:42.508 --> 01:00:45.796
has attempted to do since Jesse and Lisa fought Freddy in the real world in 1986.

01:00:45.818 --> 01:00:49.684
So Freddy is vulnerable for the first time in 15 years.

01:00:49.802 --> 01:00:52.836
They devise a plan and Katherine goes into the dream with the intention of

01:00:52.858 --> 01:00:55.540
bringing the bastard son of a hundred maniacs out with her.

01:00:55.610 --> 01:00:58.596
This dream takes her to the Temple of Morpheus, where she passes the dream demons

01:00:58.628 --> 01:01:01.896
and symbolically enters Freddy's brain, where she sees all of his

01:01:01.918 --> 01:01:05.256
memories and comes to the realization that the Springwood Slasher is none

01:01:05.288 --> 01:01:06.760
other than her Springwood father.

01:01:06.840 --> 01:01:10.700
And he's not happy about her breaking her promise to keep quiet.

01:01:10.700 --> 01:01:13.722
(IMPACT)

01:01:16.282 --> 01:01:19.173
♪ Mysterious Music ♪ 

01:01:19.520 --> 01:01:22.656
Katherine and Freddy scuffle, and she does manage to grab onto him, but he

01:01:22.678 --> 01:01:24.480
spawns in another room in the real world.

01:01:24.550 --> 01:01:27.916
At first, he appears to be human again, no longer sporting the burn scars

01:01:27.948 --> 01:01:29.488
and seemingly able to feel pain.

01:01:29.574 --> 01:01:32.848
It's never really explained, but I'm guessing this was all just part of the ruse.

01:01:32.854 --> 01:01:35.776
Because when he sees Katherine, he tries to convince her that all of

01:01:35.798 --> 01:01:38.448
the horrible things he did weren't his fault because of the abuse he

01:01:38.454 --> 01:01:39.152
suffered as a kid.

01:01:39.206 --> 01:01:42.056
He's trying to play to her sympathetic side because she's worked with so

01:01:42.078 --> 01:01:43.896
many troubled kids and felt pity for them.

01:01:43.918 --> 01:01:46.964
But what I think he's overlooking is that she was in an abusive household

01:01:47.012 --> 01:01:49.444
herself as a child, and she doesn't turn out like Freddy.

01:01:49.492 --> 01:01:51.060
She's a functioning member of society.

01:01:51.140 --> 01:01:55.076
We talk a lot about the connection between early trauma and, well, villainy

01:01:55.108 --> 01:01:57.544
here on this channel, but it's important to remember that going through

01:01:57.582 --> 01:01:59.516
stuff in your youth doesn't guarantee anything.

01:01:59.618 --> 01:02:01.912
You always have some control in your own destiny.

01:02:01.976 --> 01:02:05.324
So Katherine doesn't fall for his bit, whacks him with a nail spiked bat,

01:02:05.362 --> 01:02:07.740
and then knocks the finger blade glove off his hand.

01:02:07.810 --> 01:02:10.136
She's a switch hitter, and she's got some serious exit velo.

01:02:10.168 --> 01:02:14.048
Krueger, who somehow now has his hat back, somehow climbs onto the ceiling.

01:02:14.054 --> 01:02:17.596
Does he now have the ability to manipulate things and use his dream

01:02:17.628 --> 01:02:20.960
powers in the real world? I have a theory about that, which we'll get to.

01:02:21.030 --> 01:02:24.096
Freddy goes in for the kill, bragging that he didn't need the glove to kill

01:02:24.118 --> 01:02:24.618
her mother.

01:02:24.636 --> 01:02:26.032
She's able to head butt her way free.

01:02:26.086 --> 01:02:29.248
Then she repeatedly slashes him in the face with each strike in honor of

01:02:29.254 --> 01:02:31.170
someone close to her whose life he had taken.

01:02:31.170 --> 01:02:34.493
–[Freddy] Give me the glove! Give me the glove!

01:02:34.700 --> 01:02:38.552
You know, for someone who just said that he doesn't need the glove, he sure

01:02:38.606 --> 01:02:39.988
seems like he wants the glove.

01:02:40.084 --> 01:02:43.336
The fight and possession of the glove goes back and forth, but in the end,

01:02:43.358 --> 01:02:46.396
it is Katherine who ends up with it, and he actually encourages her to try

01:02:46.418 --> 01:02:47.468
it out for size.

01:02:47.634 --> 01:02:50.670
-[Freddy] Go ahead, put it on.

01:02:53.440 --> 01:02:55.100
-[Freddy] It's in your blood.

01:02:55.440 --> 01:02:58.156
He seems to think that wearing the glove is going to make her evil or

01:02:58.178 --> 01:02:59.632
something, but that's not what happens.

01:02:59.686 --> 01:03:00.972
She stabs him in the stomach.

01:03:01.036 --> 01:03:04.944
Then Tracy tosses her a lit stick of dynamite that they just have, and

01:03:04.982 --> 01:03:06.930
Katherine lodges it into him.

01:03:06.930 --> 01:03:08.660
–[Katherine] Happy Father’s Day.

01:03:08.660 --> 01:03:13.332
His last word is kids before he blows up, finally killing him in the real world,

01:03:13.386 --> 01:03:16.836
finally releasing the dream demons within him, and finally putting an

01:03:16.858 --> 01:03:20.084
end to the curse of Freddy Krueger that plagued Springwood for the better

01:03:20.122 --> 01:03:21.616
part of four decades.

01:03:21.728 --> 01:03:25.464
But if Freddy had the ability to use his dream abilities in the real world,

01:03:25.582 --> 01:03:29.588
how could he ever really die? My theory is that he didn't.

01:03:29.684 --> 01:03:32.280
In fact, I'm not convinced that any of this even happened.

01:03:32.350 --> 01:03:35.384
We've seen Freddy use false awakenings to trick someone into thinking

01:03:35.422 --> 01:03:38.280
they've woken up, when in fact, they're actually still in the dream world.

01:03:38.350 --> 01:03:41.976
It happened to Kristen, Alice and John, so who's to say that it didn't

01:03:42.008 --> 01:03:45.276
happen again with Katherine? What if this whole sequence where she wakes up

01:03:45.298 --> 01:03:48.796
and kills Freddy in the real world wasn't in the real world at all?

01:03:48.818 --> 01:03:52.012
We never see any follow up on any of these characters, so I have to assume

01:03:52.076 --> 01:03:52.976
that's what happened.

01:03:53.078 --> 01:03:56.816
But even if he came out victorious against Katherine, Tracy and Doc,

01:03:56.838 --> 01:03:57.776
He still had a problem.

01:03:57.878 --> 01:04:01.376
As stated early in this video, he uses the fear of children and teens to

01:04:01.398 --> 01:04:03.020
give him the power to invade dreams.

01:04:03.100 --> 01:04:06.324
And Springwood officials seemed to realize this at some point, probably

01:04:06.362 --> 01:04:09.184
because there were no kids in the entire town and rumors of Freddy Krueger

01:04:09.232 --> 01:04:11.220
invading people's dreams stopped popping up.

01:04:11.290 --> 01:04:13.936
Those who had been around long enough could have just made the connection

01:04:13.968 --> 01:04:15.404
and figured out how he operates.

01:04:15.472 --> 01:04:18.632
And at some point, these survival stories of the few who escaped, like

01:04:18.686 --> 01:04:22.216
Dr. Gordon, Alice, Yvonne and possibly Katherine, Tracy and Doc, would have

01:04:22.238 --> 01:04:23.668
started to sound more believable.

01:04:23.764 --> 01:04:27.016
So the powers that be who came to believe in Freddy Krueger took steps to

01:04:27.038 --> 01:04:29.756
ensure that he could never come back and slice through the town again.

01:04:29.858 --> 01:04:33.356
Anyone who mentioned Krueger's name would get an unfortunate diagnosis and

01:04:33.378 --> 01:04:36.348
be sentenced to treatment at Westin Hill Psychiatric Hospital, where a

01:04:36.354 --> 01:04:38.956
steady dose of the Dream suppressant medication, Hypnocil would be administered.

01:04:38.978 --> 01:04:42.192
This is the same experimental medication that Nancy used

01:04:42.246 --> 01:04:45.644
between 1981 and 1987 to stay off of Freddy's radar.

01:04:45.692 --> 01:04:46.592
And it's likely that Dr. Gordon had something to do

01:04:46.646 --> 01:04:48.848
with implementing this policy along with Springwood police.

01:04:48.934 --> 01:04:52.132
They even went back and scrubbed the public record,

01:04:52.186 --> 01:04:55.520
removing and redacting anything about Krueger and his victims.

01:04:55.600 --> 01:04:58.724
Eventually, families forgot about Springwood's curse and started moving into

01:04:58.762 --> 01:05:01.392
town again, having babies and repopulating the youth.

01:05:01.456 --> 01:05:04.496
But this new generation didn't know about the horror that plagued the town

01:05:04.528 --> 01:05:06.412
pre millennium, so they weren't afraid.

01:05:06.496 --> 01:05:09.604
There were a few hiccups along the way, like Bobby Davis and Mrs. Campbell. 

01:05:09.652 --> 01:05:12.616
But all of the deaths were staged as accidents or suicides by police.

01:05:12.638 --> 01:05:15.736
And anyone heard spouting off rhetoric about Krueger was shipped off

01:05:15.758 --> 01:05:18.588
to Western Hills and cut off from contact with the outside world.

01:05:18.674 --> 01:05:22.220
As a result, Freddy lost the power to dream crash and for the first time,

01:05:22.290 --> 01:05:23.932
found himself stuck on the outside.

01:05:24.066 --> 01:05:27.208
Before long, Freddy would make a plea with one of his contemporaries.

01:05:27.304 --> 01:05:28.824
Enter Jason Voorhees.

01:05:28.872 --> 01:05:32.396
Born in the mid 1900s in Crystal Lake, New Jersey, Jason was nearly

01:05:32.428 --> 01:05:34.448
drowned by the other kids one year at summer camp.

01:05:34.534 --> 01:05:37.516
He should have been supervised, but the counselors were off having filthy sex.

01:05:37.548 --> 01:05:40.816
So just like Freddy, Jason had a disdain for kids and teenagers, and

01:05:40.838 --> 01:05:43.204
every now and then he would come back to life and kill some of them.

01:05:43.242 --> 01:05:46.484
Jason was defeated by his niece, Jessica Kimball, and dragged down into hell,

01:05:46.522 --> 01:05:48.628
leaving his iconic hockey mask behind.

01:05:48.714 --> 01:05:52.136
It is then that Freddy reemerges and grabs the mask, hoping to make a

01:05:52.158 --> 01:05:54.020
preposition towards the Crystal Lake killer.

01:05:54.100 --> 01:05:57.780
After four years of silence, Freddy had a game plan to get back in action.

01:05:57.860 --> 01:05:58.968
-[Sheriff Williams] You listen to me.

01:05:59.054 --> 01:06:02.616
-[Sheriff Williams] We do things around here a certain way for a reason,

01:06:02.638 --> 01:06:03.940
-[Sheriff Williams] and that's given us four years of peace.

01:06:04.020 --> 01:06:07.864
Meaning that it was summer of 2005 when Freddy, most likely using the last

01:06:07.902 --> 01:06:11.176
reserves of his remaining power, takes the form of Jason's mother,

01:06:11.208 --> 01:06:14.456
Pamela Voorhees, and instructs him to wake up and go to Elm Street

01:06:14.488 --> 01:06:15.852
to strike fear into the kids now living there.

01:06:15.906 --> 01:06:18.904
Jason is immortal and can come back to life as many times as he pleases.

01:06:18.952 --> 01:06:22.224
And Freddy's plan is to have him kill and spark concerns in the town that

01:06:22.262 --> 01:06:25.072
Freddy has returned, which would give him back some of his power.

01:06:25.206 --> 01:06:29.940
-[Freddy] I’ve been away from my children for far too long.

01:06:29.940 --> 01:06:33.568
Jason makes the long walk to Springwood, and his first kill is a teenager in

01:06:33.574 --> 01:06:37.236
the upstairs bedroom at 1428 Elm Street, which is now restored to more or

01:06:37.258 --> 01:06:38.340
less how it's supposed to look.

01:06:38.410 --> 01:06:43.110
This prompts some troubling deja vu from two senior officers.

01:06:43.420 --> 01:06:46.170
-[Officer] Killed in bed? Jesus. It’s even in the same damn house.

01:06:46.780 --> 01:06:48.248
-[Officer] 1428 Elm.

01:06:48.334 --> 01:06:51.720
And that's all it takes to get the old Freddy fear train rolling again.

01:06:51.790 --> 01:06:55.416
A teen named Lori Campbell overhears the officer s ay Krueger's name, and she

01:06:55.438 --> 01:06:58.040
becomes the first person to become vulnerable to him once again.

01:06:58.110 --> 01:07:01.484
In her dream, she meets Freddy's last casualty before the fire, a little

01:07:01.522 --> 01:07:04.604
girl with empty eye sockets who cautions her that Freddy will soon be strong

01:07:04.642 --> 01:07:06.968
enough to come back and suggest that she warns people.

01:07:07.074 --> 01:07:10.528
This is obviously Freddy trying to spook her so she can cause hysteria in

01:07:10.534 --> 01:07:12.850
the real world and make the town afraid of him again.

01:07:17.460 --> 01:07:20.768
That same night, he feels confident enough to make his return and attacks a

01:07:20.774 --> 01:07:23.340
boy named Blake using a giant shadow version of himself.

01:07:23.420 --> 01:07:24.852
But the slash goes right through him.

01:07:24.906 --> 01:07:27.876
Freddy has not yet regained enough of his power to make an impact, so he

01:07:27.898 --> 01:07:29.652
sits back and lets Jason do his thing.

01:07:29.706 --> 01:07:32.836
After hearing about the new murders, two Westin Hills patients,

01:07:32.858 --> 01:07:36.144
Will and Mark,  escape and end up spreading even more hysteria about Freddy.

01:07:36.192 --> 01:07:38.628
They think that they're helping prepare people, but in reality,

01:07:38.644 --> 01:07:39.720
they're adding to Freddy's power.

01:07:39.790 --> 01:07:42.808
Lori's best friend Kia, has a nightmare where he appears in a catalog that

01:07:42.814 --> 01:07:44.664
she's flipping through and slices her nose off.

01:07:44.702 --> 01:07:47.448
But because he's not back to full strength yet, nothing manifests in the

01:07:47.454 --> 01:07:48.104
real world.

01:07:48.222 --> 01:07:51.676
But by that evening, the fear powered adrenaline that powered him through

01:07:51.698 --> 01:07:54.508
the 80s and 90s pumps through and surges once again.

01:07:54.594 --> 01:07:56.436
Freddy is ready to make his comeback.

01:07:56.488 --> 01:07:59.170
But there's one thing he didn't take into account.

01:07:59.170 --> 01:08:02.741
(IMPACT)

01:08:04.353 --> 01:08:07.965
♪ Techno Music ♪

01:08:08.180 --> 01:08:11.824
Freddy's next attempt comes that night during a cornfield dance party he

01:08:11.862 --> 01:08:14.916
appears to give the girlfriend of Jason's first Springwood victim, taking

01:08:14.938 --> 01:08:17.872
the form of her recently deceased boyfriend to lure her to a silo.

01:08:17.936 --> 01:08:18.756
Once inside, she finds herself trapped

01:08:18.778 --> 01:08:22.008
In Freddy's favorite location, the Boiler Room.

01:08:22.094 --> 01:08:25.320
Before killing her, he puts his own twist on a famous quote.

01:08:25.320 --> 01:08:29.751
–[Freddy]  The only thing to fear is fear himself.

01:08:30.060 --> 01:08:34.072
The original quote, the only thing to fear is fear itself was said by

01:08:34.126 --> 01:08:35.016
U.S. President Franklin D. Roosevelt

01:08:35.038 --> 01:08:37.732
in his inauguration speech during the Great Depression.

01:08:37.796 --> 01:08:40.988
The quote was credited with inspiring many Americans to regain faith in

01:08:40.994 --> 01:08:43.032
themselves and pull through the economic downturn.

01:08:43.096 --> 01:08:45.884
The last four years for Freddy have been like his own personal Great Depression.

01:08:45.922 --> 01:08:49.208
He hasn't haunted the nightmares of any kids, nor has he reaped

01:08:49.224 --> 01:08:49.960
any souls.

01:08:50.040 --> 01:08:53.376
But now he's pulling through, and the teens of Springwood have something to

01:08:53.398 --> 01:08:54.000
fear again.

01:08:54.070 --> 01:08:55.004
Yeah, Freddy vs. Jason, deeper than you thought. 

01:08:55.052 --> 01:08:57.836
Gibb hides in a locker,

01:08:57.868 --> 01:09:01.172
But just before Freddy gets her, a wound in her chest bursts open on its own

01:09:01.226 --> 01:09:04.550
because Jason, operating from the real world, got there first.

01:09:07.113 --> 01:09:13.063
–[Freddy] No! She’s mine! Mine! Mine!

01:09:13.400 --> 01:09:15.684
There's also an interesting parallel going on here.

01:09:15.722 --> 01:09:18.728
Freddy and Jason's feud begins because Jason moves in on a girl that he

01:09:18.734 --> 01:09:19.640
wanted to kill first.

01:09:19.710 --> 01:09:22.884
The main character this time Lori, is also caught between two boys.

01:09:22.932 --> 01:09:25.176
Tension arises because Charlie had his eyes on her.

01:09:25.198 --> 01:09:28.344
But her old boyfriend Will reemerges after escaping Westin Hills,

01:09:28.392 --> 01:09:29.436
And he had her first.

01:09:29.538 --> 01:09:30.824
Like I said, Freddy vs. Jason. 

01:09:30.872 --> 01:09:32.396
Deeper than you thought.

01:09:32.498 --> 01:09:35.736
Mark, the other Westin Hills escapee, falls asleep at his desk.

01:09:35.768 --> 01:09:39.116
And with no hypnocil to suppress his dreams, he drifts off to a scene in his

01:09:39.138 --> 01:09:41.696
bathroom where Freddy appears in the mirror, then taunts him,

01:09:41.718 --> 01:09:44.956
Using the form of his dead brother. He traps Mark in place, using barbed

01:09:44.988 --> 01:09:46.460
tendrils to tie down his feet.

01:09:46.540 --> 01:09:49.824
At first, he's willing to keep Mark alive in exchange for sending a message

01:09:49.862 --> 01:09:51.760
about Freddy's comeback to the waking world.

01:09:51.830 --> 01:09:55.504
But Mark understands his plan and refuses to help Krueger reach more victims.

01:09:55.552 --> 01:09:58.836
So Freddy, perhaps realizing that Mark's friends have arrived outside of his window, 

01:09:58.858 --> 01:10:02.116
decides to send the message himself, lighting the boy on fire and

01:10:02.138 --> 01:10:05.136
tossing him around the room in a manner similar to how he once used Tina

01:10:05.168 --> 01:10:08.216
Grey to instill fear in that early generation of Elm Street kids.

01:10:08.318 --> 01:10:11.576
He finishes Mark with a slash to the face and a message burnt into his flesh.

01:10:11.598 --> 01:10:13.064
Freddy's back.

01:10:13.182 --> 01:10:13.912
Well, no.

01:10:13.966 --> 01:10:14.904
That's Mark's back, technically.

01:10:14.942 --> 01:10:17.400
You just inscribed a message on it.

01:10:17.470 --> 01:10:20.396
Meanwhile, the Springwood Police Department is already hard at work trying

01:10:20.418 --> 01:10:23.356
to contain Freddy Krueger based on what they've learned from past cases, but

01:10:23.378 --> 01:10:25.976
not realizing that Jason Voorhees is also on the loose this time.

01:10:26.008 --> 01:10:29.244
They quarantine the town, hoping to stop the spread of talk about Freddy.

01:10:29.282 --> 01:10:32.208
Meanwhile, Lori Campbell and a group of other survivors are the

01:10:32.214 --> 01:10:34.864
first to realize that Freddy and Jason are basically in a turf war now.

01:10:34.902 --> 01:10:37.728
Lori dozes off as they're discussing their options and has a

01:10:37.734 --> 01:10:40.544
nightmare where Freddy takes the form of her father and tries to kiss her.

01:10:40.582 --> 01:10:42.864
Lucky for her, she's woken up by the others just in time.

01:10:42.902 --> 01:10:45.264
And even pulls Freddy's ear out of the dream with her.

01:10:45.302 --> 01:10:48.620
But Freddy continues to track the group as they head back to Westin Hills.

01:10:48.700 --> 01:10:51.956
There, a stoner character named Bill gets a little too sleepy, and Freddy

01:10:51.988 --> 01:10:55.016
uses the opportunity to manipulate him in his dream, making him eat this

01:10:55.038 --> 01:10:58.536
giant parasite thing, and in the real world, pour all of the hypnocil down

01:10:58.558 --> 01:10:59.058
the drain.

01:10:59.076 --> 01:11:01.652
Freddy's deductive reasoning skills here are pretty impressive.

01:11:01.716 --> 01:11:04.168
I don't believe he can see everything going on in the real world.

01:11:04.254 --> 01:11:07.028
If he could, then he would have been able to see Nancy's booby traps.

01:11:07.124 --> 01:11:10.100
But when he saw that Bill was at Westin Hills, he made the connection,

01:11:10.180 --> 01:11:11.992
figured out their plan and thwarted it.

01:11:12.046 --> 01:11:15.368
He also uses this opportunity to get back at Jason, who had shown up to try

01:11:15.374 --> 01:11:16.716
to steal another one of his kills.

01:11:16.748 --> 01:11:20.096
Freddy takes over Bill's body and sedates him using a tranquilizer known as

01:11:20.118 --> 01:11:23.520
Imobitine because every medication in this facility has extremely obvious

01:11:23.590 --> 01:11:24.684
naming conventions.

01:11:24.812 --> 01:11:28.224
Unfortunately for him, this gives Jason enough time to chop Bill in half

01:11:28.262 --> 01:11:29.532
before he can devour the soul.

01:11:29.596 --> 01:11:32.444
But from Freddy's point of view, it's probably a worthwhile sacrifice.

01:11:32.492 --> 01:11:35.232
He got rid of the hypnocil and pacified his new rival.

01:11:35.296 --> 01:11:38.084
Earlier, I mentioned how it didn't make sense for a character to dream while

01:11:38.122 --> 01:11:39.748
knocked out cold, but this is different.

01:11:39.834 --> 01:11:42.564
It's understood to be possible to dream while sedated, even under anesthesia. 

01:11:42.602 --> 01:11:46.388
So for the first time, Jason finds himself in the old boiler

01:11:46.404 --> 01:11:47.828
room using the appearance of Mrs. Voorhees. 

01:11:47.844 --> 01:11:51.144
Freddy scolds Jason for not returning back home after killing off a few teens, 

01:11:51.182 --> 01:11:54.964
then reveals himself as Freddy Krueger and the two icons clash

01:11:55.012 --> 01:11:56.488
head to head for the first time.

01:11:56.574 --> 01:11:59.436
Being that Freddy can't take damage in the dream world, he's got the home

01:11:59.458 --> 01:12:01.310
field advantage in this face off.

01:12:01.310 --> 01:12:03.360
– [Freddy]Welcome to my nightmare.&nbsp;

01:12:03.360 --> 01:12:06.860
And he also air yeets Jason a bunch of times, which is pretty funny.

01:12:10.960 --> 01:12:14.224
Freddy loves air yeeting Jason and really all of their surroundings during

01:12:14.262 --> 01:12:14.768
this fight.

01:12:14.854 --> 01:12:16.400
We've never really seen him do this before.

01:12:16.470 --> 01:12:19.196
It's hard to say if this is a new technique that he's developed or if he's

01:12:19.228 --> 01:12:20.256
always been able to do this.

01:12:20.278 --> 01:12:23.180
And this time he's just keeping his distance because he knows that Jason

01:12:23.260 --> 01:12:25.840
poses more of a threat than the average Springwood final girl.

01:12:25.910 --> 01:12:28.864
Whatever the reason may be, the part where he freaking sends Jason across

01:12:28.902 --> 01:12:32.961
the room by air humping has gotta be one of the most under appreciated moments of all time.

01:12:33.126 --> 01:12:36.833
Like if you type in ‘air humping Freddy’ into YouTube, the only results you get are

01:12:36.833 --> 01:12:39.689
Fred Jones and Freddy Fazbear and for some reason Kermit.

01:12:42.060 --> 01:12:45.528
But even dropping a water tank on Jason doesn't do him in, which starts to

01:12:45.534 --> 01:12:47.156
frustrate his nightmarish opponents.

01:12:47.188 --> 01:12:50.316
But it does lead to him discovering Jason's greatest fear, water.

01:12:50.418 --> 01:12:53.688
It causes him to revert back to that trembling little boy at Crystal Lake,

01:12:53.704 --> 01:12:57.628
and Freddy dives deeper into his subconscious, pun not intended, again, surprisingly.

01:12:57.714 --> 01:13:01.452
He's taken back to Jason's childhood the moment the other kids

01:13:01.506 --> 01:13:02.332
threw him in the lake.

01:13:02.396 --> 01:13:05.776
Lori enters the dream, hoping to bring Krueger out with her, the idea being

01:13:05.798 --> 01:13:08.656
that Jason could kill Freddy in the real world and hopefully not come back

01:13:08.678 --> 01:13:09.404
to Springwood.

01:13:09.452 --> 01:13:13.056
But before she can save young Jason from a watery grave, Freddy emerges and

01:13:13.078 --> 01:13:13.804
pulls him under.

01:13:13.862 --> 01:13:14.592
Even deeper.

01:13:14.656 --> 01:13:17.652
Timing is not on his side, though, and Jason's tranquilizer wears off,

01:13:17.706 --> 01:13:19.712
waking him up and vanishing him from the nightmare.

01:13:19.776 --> 01:13:22.836
In a rage, he turns his fury to Lori, who tries to pull him out of the dream,

01:13:22.858 --> 01:13:25.956
but thanks to another false awakening, finds herself in her own nightmare,

01:13:25.978 --> 01:13:28.916
where the truth is revealed about Freddy being the one who killed

01:13:28.948 --> 01:13:29.460
her mother.

01:13:29.540 --> 01:13:33.048
After taking her out, he comes after Lori, but once again, time is not on

01:13:33.054 --> 01:13:36.088
his side, and it would probably help if he just killed his victims as soon

01:13:36.094 --> 01:13:39.036
as he got the chance, instead of just hovering over them and talking to them

01:13:39.058 --> 01:13:39.708
for two minutes.

01:13:39.794 --> 01:13:41.196
But that's not what he does.

01:13:41.298 --> 01:13:44.808
The two awake in a flaming cabin in Camp Crystal Lake, with Jason marching

01:13:44.824 --> 01:13:45.976
towards them in a rage.

01:13:46.088 --> 01:13:49.180
Being in the real world, Jason poses a real threat to Freddy now.

01:13:49.250 --> 01:13:52.704
And like the Milwaukee Brewers, anytime they have to play my Cubs,

01:13:52.742 --> 01:13:54.188
he's also lost his home field advantage.

01:13:54.284 --> 01:13:58.208
Their epic battle tears the cabin apart, but somehow Freddy sneaks away from

01:13:58.214 --> 01:14:01.040
the chaos to try to nab Lori and her friends before they can get away.

01:14:01.110 --> 01:14:04.144
I like to think that he realizes that he's no match for Jason in the real world

01:14:04.182 --> 01:14:07.148
and needs their soul power to buff him up to take on his masked opponent.

01:14:07.164 --> 01:14:10.864
However, it's not long until Jason finds him and steals yet

01:14:10.902 --> 01:14:13.608
another other one of his victims, and the two duke it out some more.

01:14:13.694 --> 01:14:16.868
The fight finds its way to a construction site, where Freddy launches gas

01:14:16.884 --> 01:14:20.276
tank torpedoes, releases metal stakes, and manages to get them both struck

01:14:20.308 --> 01:14:21.732
by a runaway storage cart.

01:14:21.796 --> 01:14:25.208
But Jason is a relentless machine, and Freddy continues to find ways to

01:14:25.214 --> 01:14:25.848
fight back.

01:14:25.934 --> 01:14:29.148
It probably could have gone on forever, but in the end, Lori and her

01:14:29.154 --> 01:14:32.728
boyfriend, Will douse the dock in propane and come back with torches, setting

01:14:32.744 --> 01:14:35.480
the dock ablaze and triggering a massive explosion.

01:14:35.560 --> 01:14:38.556
Just as he had during his first trip through the real world, Freddy is

01:14:38.578 --> 01:14:41.404
torched by Elm Street residents, but this time, it's only briefly.

01:14:41.452 --> 01:14:44.544
He falls into the lake, extinguishing the flames, and shortly after comes

01:14:44.582 --> 01:14:46.604
for the two surviving teens with Jason's machete.

01:14:46.652 --> 01:14:49.936
But with the last of his energy, Jason stabs him through the back with his

01:14:49.958 --> 01:14:53.328
own finger bladed arm, giving Lori the opportunity to avenge her fallen

01:14:53.344 --> 01:14:56.704
mother and friends with one clean, decapitating slice.

01:14:56.832 --> 01:15:00.644
At long last, Nancy Thompson's original goal of killing Freddy in the real

01:15:00.682 --> 01:15:01.840
world has been achieved.

01:15:01.920 --> 01:15:06.352
But is this truly the end of Freddy Krueger? The evidence would suggest no,

01:15:06.426 --> 01:15:09.288
as the last thing we see is Jason emerging from the lake with the

01:15:09.294 --> 01:15:10.632
dismembered Freddy head in hand.

01:15:10.686 --> 01:15:14.264
But he seems to have the same unrelenting ability to survive in this world

01:15:14.302 --> 01:15:17.240
as he did in the nightmarescape of his many victims.

01:15:17.320 --> 01:15:20.332
Remember to subscribe to CZ's World for new horrors every week.

01:15:20.386 --> 01:15:23.532
Ring the Deathbell for notifications, and I'll see you in the next one.

01:15:23.586 --> 01:15:25.420
Assuming we both survive.

01:15:27.840 --> 01:15:29.870
Food. I want food.

01:15:30.480 --> 01:15:32.480
So I finished recording the Freddy video.

01:15:32.630 --> 01:15:33.888
I think it'll be pretty good.

01:15:33.974 --> 01:15:36.850
There were definitely parts that were less fun to talk about than others.

01:15:37.300 --> 01:15:39.644
Well, because the fun part is analyzing the characters.

01:15:39.772 --> 01:15:41.240
Some of those later sequels.

01:15:41.340 --> 01:15:43.540
Not a whole lot of substance to talk about, really.

01:15:43.690 --> 01:15:45.652
Honestly. Pretty hard to get through.

01:15:45.786 --> 01:15:46.416
Freddy vs. Jason

01:15:46.448 --> 01:15:48.230
is surprisingly deep, though.

01:15:49.400 --> 01:15:50.564
Yeah, I don't know.

01:15:50.602 --> 01:15:53.236
The one problem that I kept running into was the rules are constantly

01:15:53.268 --> 01:15:54.948
changing from movie to movie.

01:15:55.124 --> 01:15:58.010
It does kind of feel like something's missing, though.

01:16:04.140 --> 01:16:04.638
-[News Reporter] Right now.

01:16:04.638 --> 01:16:08.344
-[News Reporter] We have some breaking news here this morning, a first on first.

01:16:08.462 --> 01:16:09.604
-[News Reporter] The USGS is reporting a

01:16:09.652 --> 01:16:14.840
-[News Reporter] Magnitude 4.2 earthquake off the coast of Malibu, California.

01:16:57.910 --> 01:16:59.380
There's one more thing.

01:16:59.380 --> 01:17:02.112
(IMPACT)

01:17:04.799 --> 01:17:08.230
 ♪ Mysterious Music ♪

01:17:08.230 --> 01:17:11.326
I think I figured out why the rules change so much in the Elm Street franchise.

01:17:11.358 --> 01:17:14.518
At first I was bothered by this, but I've come to realize the

01:17:14.524 --> 01:17:15.590
answer is right there.

01:17:15.660 --> 01:17:18.962
It's because a Nightmare on Elm Street, Freddy's Revenge, Dream Warriors,

01:17:19.026 --> 01:17:22.274
the Dream Master, The Dream Child, Freddy's Dead and Freddy vs. Jason

01:17:22.322 --> 01:17:25.154
Are technically movies within a franchise.

01:17:25.282 --> 01:17:28.054
They're just movies made to entertain characters in a movie.

01:17:28.102 --> 01:17:30.022
They weren't made to be inspected that closely.

01:17:30.086 --> 01:17:32.826
It's not that different from when I inspect newspaper headlines about

01:17:32.848 --> 01:17:35.814
Freddy's kidnappings, but the articles themselves talk about baseball scores

01:17:35.862 --> 01:17:40.154
-[Announcer] Frederick, Freddy

01:17:40.282 --> 01:17:43.518
And Marine corp movements. The real world in this franchise is actually the world

01:17:43.524 --> 01:17:46.618
where actors like Heather Langencamp and Robert Englund star in

01:17:46.634 --> 01:17:47.530
A Nightmare on Elm Street movies in Hollywood.

01:17:47.610 --> 01:17:50.974
Mrs. Langencamp's son even takes a shot at the increasingly unbelievable

01:17:51.022 --> 01:17:53.118
logic seen in some of the Elm Street sequels.

01:17:53.214 --> 01:17:58.942
-[Dylan] Can you come with me in my dreams? 
-[Heather] I think that only happens in the movies.

01:17:59.086 --> 01:18:00.142
In terms of the timeline,

01:18:00.206 --> 01:18:03.126
This takes place in the modern day of when New Nightmare came out, which is 1994.

01:18:03.148 --> 01:18:06.626
After Freddy's Dead, but before Freddy vs. Jason.

01:18:06.738 --> 01:18:11.186
-[Reporter] So Heather approaching the 10th anniversary of this whole

01:18:11.218 --> 01:18:11.750
-[Reporter] Nightmare on Elm Street thing.

01:18:11.820 --> 01:18:14.866
The horror is set in motion when Wes Craven, the director of the original

01:18:14.898 --> 01:18:17.818
Nightmare on Elm Street, starts developing an idea for a revival of the franchise. 

01:18:17.824 --> 01:18:21.338
Even he isn't fully in control of the script, claiming that he

01:18:21.344 --> 01:18:24.266
just waits for scary dreams to come to him, and then he writes them down and

01:18:24.288 --> 01:18:25.162
incorporates them.

01:18:25.216 --> 01:18:28.394
He describes a nightmare entity so ancient that it's existed in many

01:18:28.432 --> 01:18:29.670
different forms and cultures.

01:18:29.750 --> 01:18:31.962
The only ones that can capture it are storytellers.

01:18:32.026 --> 01:18:34.458
It was captured for the last decade in the Nightmare on Elm Street franchise,

01:18:34.474 --> 01:18:37.006
but when the series ended, it was set free.

01:18:37.108 --> 01:18:41.106
-[Wes] He's sort of gotten used to being Freddy now, and he likes our time and space.

01:18:41.128 --> 01:18:46.350
-[Wes] So he has decided to cross over. Out of films into our reality.

01:18:46.430 --> 01:18:49.858
After he begins writing, Heather begins receiving ominous phone calls from a

01:18:49.864 --> 01:18:52.798
stalker with the Freddy Krueger voice repeating the lines of the in uiverse

01:18:52.814 --> 01:18:56.034
nursery rhyme, which weighs heavily on her and freaks out her son Dylan.

01:18:56.082 --> 01:18:59.158
She also receives a series of troubling letters burned into book pages in

01:18:59.164 --> 01:18:59.650
the mail.

01:18:59.650 --> 01:19:02.726
One day, she has a dream that the animatronic Freddy glove, used in a new

01:19:02.748 --> 01:19:05.954
Nightmare on Elm Street movie seems to come to life on its own and massacres

01:19:06.002 --> 01:19:08.250
the crew members on set before coming for her son.

01:19:08.320 --> 01:19:10.986
At first she believes the nightmare was triggered by an earthquake, but

01:19:11.008 --> 01:19:13.526
would soon come to suspect a much darker explanation.

01:19:13.638 --> 01:19:16.538
During one talk show interview, the host surprises Heather with an

01:19:16.544 --> 01:19:19.258
appearance from her Nightmare co star Robert Englund, complete with the

01:19:19.264 --> 01:19:20.442
Freddy makeup and costume.

01:19:20.506 --> 01:19:23.326
She plays along, but she's clearly pretty uncomfortable because of what

01:19:23.348 --> 01:19:24.878
she's going through in her personal life.

01:19:24.964 --> 01:19:28.226
She comes home to discover Dylan having an episode, and when she rushes into

01:19:28.248 --> 01:19:30.020
his room, he says this...

01:19:30.020 --> 01:19:37.474
-[Dylan] Never sleep again. Never sleep again.

01:19:38.150 --> 01:19:41.298
Which is the final line from the Freddy Krueger nursery rhyme,

01:19:41.304 --> 01:19:42.690
a movie that she had forbidden him from watching.

01:19:42.760 --> 01:19:46.018
She also discovers a four fingered slash through one of his toys, causing

01:19:46.034 --> 01:19:49.174
her to start to suspect Freddy Krueger may be crossing over into the real world.

01:19:49.212 --> 01:19:52.598
Later that night, Dylan expresses a belief that Rex keeps away the

01:19:52.604 --> 01:19:54.050
mean old man with the claws.

01:19:54.130 --> 01:19:56.986
She insists that there's nothing under his bed, but it's hard to tell if

01:19:57.008 --> 01:19:59.686
she's trying to convince him or trying to convince herself.

01:19:59.798 --> 01:20:03.078
This is also a reversal of the circumstances from her role as Nancy Thompson

01:20:03.094 --> 01:20:04.294
in Nightmare on Elm Street.

01:20:04.342 --> 01:20:07.226
In that movie, she believed in Freddy, but had a hard time getting any

01:20:07.248 --> 01:20:09.338
support from any parents or authority figures.

01:20:09.434 --> 01:20:12.382
Now she's in the position of the parent grappling with whether to believe

01:20:12.436 --> 01:20:14.842
her own kid, at risk of giving into the hysteria.

01:20:14.906 --> 01:20:16.474
After hearing about Dylan's episode.

01:20:16.522 --> 01:20:19.726
His father, Chase, a special effects artist doing pre-production for the

01:20:19.748 --> 01:20:22.546
New Nightmare movie, attempts to rush home from the location, but ends up

01:20:22.568 --> 01:20:25.794
passing out during the long drive or at least getting drowsy enough to enter

01:20:25.832 --> 01:20:29.106
that state of Hypnogogic hallucination the same way that Nancy did as her

01:20:29.128 --> 01:20:30.194
body started to shut down near the end of A Nightmare on Elm Street. 

01:20:30.232 --> 01:20:33.646
Freddy's arm emerges from Chase's seat and

01:20:33.678 --> 01:20:36.550
stabs him in the chest, sending him barreling into a wall.

01:20:36.620 --> 01:20:39.426
Apparently they didn't show him the same documentary that my class was shown

01:20:39.458 --> 01:20:42.390
in film school to warn against the dangers of sleep deprivation.

01:20:42.390 --> 01:20:46.592
♪ Who needs sleep! Who needs sleep! ♪ 

01:20:46.910 --> 01:20:51.002
Say what you want about it, but that song was so annoying that it stuck and

01:20:51.056 --> 01:20:52.026
nobody ever drove home drowsy.

01:20:52.048 --> 01:20:55.626
As it often goes in the movies, Chase's injuries are attributed to

01:20:55.648 --> 01:20:58.458
damage caused by the vehicle, as it would be ridiculous to suspect a

01:20:58.464 --> 01:20:59.898
supernatural movie character.

01:20:59.994 --> 01:21:03.166
During the funeral, an earthquake shakes her husband's coffin loose and she

01:21:03.188 --> 01:21:04.234
hits her head in the commotion.

01:21:04.282 --> 01:21:07.418
This causes her to have a short dream where Dylan disappears and she finds

01:21:07.434 --> 01:21:10.542
him in the burial plot being dragged to hell by Freddy Krueger again.

01:21:10.596 --> 01:21:13.534
It probably isn't possible to dream while you're knocked unconscious, but

01:21:13.572 --> 01:21:16.446
maybe this time the dream occurred as she was coming back too, because the

01:21:16.468 --> 01:21:18.622
head trauma doesn't look as serious.

01:21:18.676 --> 01:21:21.798
The night, Dylan seems to be in a trance, standing in front of the TV,

01:21:21.804 --> 01:21:22.834
watching A Nightmare on Elm Street.

01:21:22.882 --> 01:21:25.558
It appears that he's sleepwalking, and most likely in the midst of a nightmare,

01:21:25.564 --> 01:21:27.942
 based on his reaction when his mom wakes him up.

01:21:27.996 --> 01:21:30.774
When asked where he heard the Freddy nursery rhyme, he claims that he heard

01:21:30.812 --> 01:21:32.134
it from under his bed.

01:21:32.252 --> 01:21:36.950
-[Dylan] Trying to get up. Trying to get up into our world.

01:21:37.100 --> 01:21:39.926
The devil comparison that I made through the first four Elm Street films

01:21:39.958 --> 01:21:43.146
that kind of faded away after that is back in a very bold way when it comes

01:21:43.168 --> 01:21:44.630
to this version of Freddy Krueger.

01:21:44.710 --> 01:21:47.606
Freddy seems to take hold of Dylan again the next day at the playground.

01:21:47.638 --> 01:21:51.934
And can I just say, why is climbing on this thing even an option?

01:21:51.972 --> 01:21:55.086
Who designed this? And Dylan almost seems to be mimicking what happened to

01:21:55.108 --> 01:21:56.986
Philip Anderson from A Nightmare on Elm Street 3: Dream Warriors

01:21:57.018 --> 01:21:59.966
the only Elm Street film outside of the original that

01:21:59.988 --> 01:22:01.166
Heather Langencamp was in.

01:22:01.188 --> 01:22:04.242
It's almost as if Freddy is trying to use her past memories against her.

01:22:04.296 --> 01:22:06.142
As they say, the devil's in the details.

01:22:06.206 --> 01:22:09.554
Nancy and her costar, John Saxon, are able to run over and catch the boy

01:22:09.592 --> 01:22:12.626
before he falls to the same fate that Philip did, but he still seems to be

01:22:12.648 --> 01:22:13.950
entranced afterwards.

01:22:14.110 --> 01:22:17.030
-[Dylan] God wouldn't take me.

01:22:17.100 --> 01:22:20.038
But the devil would. As Heather would find out that night when Freddy's claws

01:22:20.044 --> 01:22:21.282
poke through the fabric of her own reality.

01:22:21.346 --> 01:22:24.578
But unlike in A Nightmare on Elm Street, this time he really is crossing

01:22:24.594 --> 01:22:25.854
over into her own reality.

01:22:25.922 --> 01:22:29.546
A loud crash from downstairs wakes her up, but evidence of his intrusion is there,

01:22:29.546 --> 01:22:32.581
just as it was in Tina gray's pajamas a decade prior.

01:22:32.870 --> 01:22:36.198
Upon investigating the noise downstairs, she finds her son has now fashioned

01:22:36.214 --> 01:22:39.646
his own Freddy Krueger glove using kitchen knives, and he attacks her with it.

01:22:39.668 --> 01:22:42.202
Thankfully for her, this was also a dream.

01:22:42.266 --> 01:22:45.518
The longer Heather stays idle, the closer Freddy gets to the real world.

01:22:45.604 --> 01:22:48.366
During one of his mysterious phone calls, his tongue comes through the

01:22:48.388 --> 01:22:49.790
phone, just like in Nightmare One.

01:22:49.860 --> 01:22:52.974
Heather visits Wes Craven and he tells her that she's a gatekeeper.

01:22:53.022 --> 01:22:55.362
The only person who can prevent Freddy from crossing over.

01:22:55.416 --> 01:22:57.790
The only way she can do this is by being in the movie.

01:22:57.870 --> 01:23:00.030
Only a storyteller can capture his essence.

01:23:00.110 --> 01:23:03.006
He may be telling the truth, but the method for stopping Freddy falls

01:23:03.038 --> 01:23:05.546
suspiciously in line with his motives as a film director.

01:23:05.598 --> 01:23:08.294
It would be like if the brands I work with told me that the only way to save

01:23:08.332 --> 01:23:11.698
my family is to promote their audiobook service or meal delivery kits.

01:23:11.794 --> 01:23:14.934
Things get even more real when Freddy takes the lives of two more special

01:23:14.972 --> 01:23:17.478
effects artists who'd been prepping for the movie, and the animatronic

01:23:17.494 --> 01:23:18.662
Freddy glove goes missing.

01:23:18.726 --> 01:23:20.662
Eventually, Heather's fears are confirmed.

01:23:20.726 --> 01:23:24.238
After being rocked by another big earthquake, she investigates a noise in

01:23:24.244 --> 01:23:25.150
her closet.

01:23:25.486 --> 01:23:27.234
-[Freddy] Miss me?

01:23:27.606 --> 01:23:30.640
(IMPACT)

01:23:32.211 --> 01:23:35.970
♪ Haunting Music ♪

01:23:35.970 --> 01:23:39.274
Heather's attempted escape from Freddy Krueger results in her being wrestled

01:23:39.322 --> 01:23:39.982
onto her bed.

01:23:40.036 --> 01:23:43.362
More and more, her scenes as Nancy Thompson in the original movie are coming true.

01:23:43.416 --> 01:23:45.662
Freddy even refers to her as Nancy at one point.

01:23:45.726 --> 01:23:49.342
Another earthquake shakes her awake, but she isn't unscathed.

01:23:49.406 --> 01:23:52.114
She tries to stay with her son as long as possible at the hospital, but

01:23:52.152 --> 01:23:55.602
grows exhausted, leading to increasing dreams and hallucinations of Freddy.

01:23:55.666 --> 01:23:58.774
Because of this, he continually gets closer to crossing over into the real world.

01:23:58.812 --> 01:24:01.894
A Nightmare on Elm Street played with the idea of blurring the line

01:24:01.932 --> 01:24:03.170
between dream and reality.

01:24:03.250 --> 01:24:06.566
As Nancy became more sleep deprived, she started to experience her nightmare

01:24:06.598 --> 01:24:07.370
in the real world.

01:24:07.440 --> 01:24:10.886
This mirrored her troubling home situation, where her mother's alcohol abuse

01:24:10.918 --> 01:24:14.106
blurred her own lines of reality in a constant limbo between sobriety and drunkenness. 

01:24:14.128 --> 01:24:17.706
Now Heather has grown up and she's experiencing a new form of

01:24:17.728 --> 01:24:18.470
blurred reality.

01:24:18.550 --> 01:24:21.534
Losing sight of the line between fiction and the real world,

01:24:21.572 --> 01:24:24.734
She increasingly starts to see scenes that she's acted in taking hold in her own life,

01:24:24.772 --> 01:24:27.650
like when she goes to find where Dylan is being treated.

01:24:27.650 --> 01:24:28.860
– Nurse] Do you have a pass?

01:24:28.860 --> 01:24:29.669
–[Nancy] Screw your pass.

01:24:29.669 --> 01:24:31.000
–[Hall Monitor] Where’s your pass?

01:24:31.000 --> 01:24:32.150
–[Nancy] Screw your pass.

01:24:32.150 --> 01:24:34.942
Dylan is moved to a room for special care and sedated.

01:24:35.006 --> 01:24:38.098
Although his babysitter tries to keep him awake, he becomes drowsy enough to

01:24:38.104 --> 01:24:40.978
see Freddy Krueger appear behind her and gore her in the back.

01:24:41.064 --> 01:24:44.226
She's lifted into the air, much like Tina was in A Nightmare on Elm Street,

01:24:44.258 --> 01:24:46.994
and Dylan witnesses the horrific murder of his babysitter.

01:24:47.042 --> 01:24:50.178
Freddy comes for him next, but Dylan is also a sleepwalker and he's

01:24:50.194 --> 01:24:51.202
determined to escape.

01:24:51.266 --> 01:24:54.438
The chase, takes him across a busy freeway where a deity like Freddy of the Skies

01:24:54.444 --> 01:24:56.254
nearly turns him into roadkill.

01:24:56.322 --> 01:24:58.938
Then an entire Krueger army chases him back home.

01:24:59.024 --> 01:25:01.866
His mother is relieved to finally catch up with him there, but they're also

01:25:01.888 --> 01:25:05.606
visited by a concerned friend, John Saxon, who played Nancy Thompson's dad

01:25:05.638 --> 01:25:06.182
in the movie.

01:25:06.246 --> 01:25:09.618
He too starts calling her Nancy, seemingly having turned into his character

01:25:09.654 --> 01:25:10.282
from the film.

01:25:10.346 --> 01:25:13.566
Heather refuses to play along at first, but she continues to see more and

01:25:13.588 --> 01:25:16.446
more of the movie coming true before her eyes, until eventually she just

01:25:16.468 --> 01:25:18.810
caves in and decides to play Nancy Thompson.

01:25:18.890 --> 01:25:21.658
-[Nancy] I love you too, Daddy.

01:25:21.754 --> 01:25:25.502
And in any other scenario, calling your co-worker Daddy while off the job

01:25:25.556 --> 01:25:28.394
might raise a few eyebrows, even if you are a professional actor.

01:25:28.442 --> 01:25:31.186
But this represents Heather playing the character, which is what

01:25:31.218 --> 01:25:33.394
Wes Craven told her she would need to do to stop Freddy.

01:25:33.442 --> 01:25:35.830
-[Wes] I think the only way to stop him is to make another movie.

01:25:36.170 --> 01:25:38.546
-[Wes] Now, I swear to you, I'm going to stay by this computer

01:25:38.578 --> 01:25:39.554
-[Wes] And keep writing until I finish the script.

01:25:39.602 --> 01:25:42.614
We can assume that this is where he finally reaches and kidnaps the boy,

01:25:42.652 --> 01:25:45.746
just as he had in the movies, bringing him to his lair with plans to harvest

01:25:45.778 --> 01:25:46.470
his soul there.

01:25:46.540 --> 01:25:49.594
Because when Heather returns to the house, which has now transformed into

01:25:49.632 --> 01:25:53.526
1428 elm street, Dylan is nowhere to be found, only a trail of sleeping

01:25:53.558 --> 01:25:54.634
pills that he refused to take

01:25:54.672 --> 01:25:55.350
At the hospital.

01:25:55.430 --> 01:25:59.086
She realizes what she must do follow Nancy's footsteps by going into the

01:25:59.108 --> 01:26:00.458
dream to face Krueger.

01:26:00.554 --> 01:26:03.562
She slides into the world of dreams, where she's spit out of a giant under worldly,

01:26:03.626 --> 01:26:06.890
Freddy Krueger shrine that drops her into a deep pit.

01:26:06.970 --> 01:26:10.058
She lands in a pool surrounded by Doric columns where there are only two

01:26:10.084 --> 01:26:13.586
sources of light the heavenly luminescence shining down from above and the

01:26:13.608 --> 01:26:16.590
warm glow of the hellish fires that surround this safe zone.

01:26:16.670 --> 01:26:19.746
The scene looks like something mythological somewhere you would expect an

01:26:19.768 --> 01:26:22.078
ancient tale of gods and demons to unfold.

01:26:22.174 --> 01:26:25.606
Since Freddy's emergence, Dylan has been trying to reach god to protect him

01:26:25.628 --> 01:26:28.066
from the devil that is masquerading as Freddy Krueger.

01:26:28.178 --> 01:26:33.074
-[Dylan] Why does god let there be bad things?

01:26:33.122 --> 01:26:36.722
But when no god came to his rescue, heather had to take things into her own hands and realize that divine role.

01:26:36.786 --> 01:26:40.458
Freddy stalks her from just beyond her field of vision, just as Nancy had in

01:26:40.464 --> 01:26:41.830
the boiler room in Elm Street.

01:26:41.910 --> 01:26:44.778
Her search for Dylan brings her to this sort of greek temple in the underworld, 

01:26:44.784 --> 01:26:47.878
where she discovers frieses of terrifying looking entities,

01:26:47.974 --> 01:26:50.878
perhaps other forms that the dream demon has taken over the years.

01:26:50.964 --> 01:26:54.506
At one point, she nearly backs into a giant stone bowl with the word lethe on it.

01:26:54.538 --> 01:26:57.546
Referring to lethe, one of the five rivers of the underworld in Greek mythology. 

01:26:57.578 --> 01:27:00.606
It was believed that when souls died and entered the underworld, 

01:27:00.628 --> 01:27:03.406
they would drink from the waters of the river lethe to forget

01:27:03.438 --> 01:27:05.054
their earthly lives and memories.

01:27:05.182 --> 01:27:08.674
This also ties in with the idea of Heather leaving her earthly life behind

01:27:08.712 --> 01:27:11.726
to take on the role of a god and find and rescue her son from Freddy Krueger.

01:27:11.758 --> 01:27:14.654
Dylan finds her, but then so does Freddy.

01:27:14.702 --> 01:27:17.746
He throws her into a pot, which shatters and she's left lying in a shallow

01:27:17.778 --> 01:27:20.038
pool of snakes, which he tries to force her head into.

01:27:20.124 --> 01:27:21.970
The snakes are also a biblical reference.

01:27:22.050 --> 01:27:24.882
The original Nightmare on Elm Street features many examples of characters

01:27:24.946 --> 01:27:27.866
trying to turn to christianity to save them, but to no avail.

01:27:27.968 --> 01:27:31.466
Christianity holds this concept of the original sin, where Adam and Eve were

01:27:31.488 --> 01:27:34.774
instructed not to eat the forbidden fruits, but Eve was tempted by a serpent

01:27:34.822 --> 01:27:37.350
who is often interpreted as a representation of the devil.

01:27:37.430 --> 01:27:41.146
The idea is to teach that sin is an inherently human trait, so Freddy

01:27:41.178 --> 01:27:43.934
pushing her face down into the serpents is meant to make her feel less

01:27:43.972 --> 01:27:45.070
divine and more human.

01:27:45.140 --> 01:27:48.286
But Heather uses his attack against him, grabbing one of the snakes by its

01:27:48.308 --> 01:27:49.930
head and forcing it into his eye.

01:27:50.010 --> 01:27:51.306
Nancy is the gatekeeper.

01:27:51.338 --> 01:27:54.178
She's not going to be the one to sin, but she'll gladly wait for Freddy to

01:27:54.184 --> 01:27:54.958
make a mistake.

01:27:55.054 --> 01:27:58.178
She also delivers a pretty solid punch to the face and beats him with a torch.

01:27:58.184 --> 01:28:01.166
Torches are another symbolic artifact when it comes to Greek mythology,

01:28:01.198 --> 01:28:04.642
often seen as a connection between the mortal world and the gods.

01:28:04.706 --> 01:28:08.086
For example, Prometheus was the god of fire who stole fire from the gods of Olympus 

01:28:08.108 --> 01:28:09.778
and gifted it to humanity.

01:28:09.874 --> 01:28:12.806
One tradition that still exists today is the passing of the torch at

01:28:12.828 --> 01:28:15.926
competitions such as the Olympics, which symbolizes the continuity of

01:28:15.948 --> 01:28:18.746
tradition and the connection between the athletes and the gods,

01:28:18.768 --> 01:28:21.078
as the Olympics were considered a sacred event by the Greeks.

01:28:21.174 --> 01:28:24.246
But there's also a double meaning here, because Freddy Krueger was burned

01:28:24.278 --> 01:28:27.578
alive by the Elm Street parents, some might say torched in the world of the movies,

01:28:27.584 --> 01:28:31.086
but even this doesn't prevent him from getting the upper hand in

01:28:31.108 --> 01:28:34.014
pinning Heather to a stone tablet with the word Lust written on it.

01:28:34.052 --> 01:28:37.594
A surefire callback to the intimate subtext present between Krueger and Nancy

01:28:37.642 --> 01:28:38.158
on the screen.

01:28:38.244 --> 01:28:41.346
It's part of a greater display of the seven deadly sins, again calling back

01:28:41.368 --> 01:28:43.710
to the idea of conflating humanity with sin.

01:28:43.790 --> 01:28:47.154
Lucky for her, Dylan comes to the rescue, stabbing Freddy in the leg before

01:28:47.192 --> 01:28:48.050
scampering away.

01:28:48.120 --> 01:28:51.746
He tosses Heather aside and chases Dylan to this furnace she's knocked out momentarily, 

01:28:51.768 --> 01:28:54.594
but eventually runs to the sounds of her child's distress,

01:28:54.642 --> 01:28:57.846
where she's slowed down by this ground slop on the stairs, just like what

01:28:57.868 --> 01:29:00.966
Nancy found herself stuck in on the stairs at the Elm Street house.

01:29:01.068 --> 01:29:04.934
Freddy uses his extended arms to reach and grab the boy, then, in a move

01:29:04.972 --> 01:29:07.946
that we've never seen in the movies, stretches his mouth open to an

01:29:07.968 --> 01:29:10.698
impossible size with the intention of devouring him whole.

01:29:10.784 --> 01:29:13.734
A new twist on the concept of consuming his victim's soul.

01:29:13.782 --> 01:29:17.174
But with half of Dylan's head engulfed in Freddy's gaping mouth,

01:29:17.222 --> 01:29:20.366
Heather arrives and stabs her rival in the back, allowing Dylan to

01:29:20.388 --> 01:29:21.598
get loose as Freddy rithes in pain.

01:29:21.684 --> 01:29:24.490
This time, Dylan is the one to face imagery of a snake.

01:29:24.570 --> 01:29:27.226
Meanwhile, his mother remains vicious with the knife.

01:29:27.338 --> 01:29:30.426
She can be seen pulling the blade right out of Freddy's crotch, something

01:29:30.468 --> 01:29:33.826
that no amount of pain tolerance can prepare you for, and perhaps the

01:29:33.848 --> 01:29:37.618
longtime coming revenge for the years of child abuse and molestation...

01:29:37.624 --> 01:29:38.594
In the movies at least.

01:29:38.712 --> 01:29:42.766
Even after this, Freddy still manages to recuperate one more time, shooting

01:29:42.798 --> 01:29:46.118
out his tongue, which wraps around her head the fifth and final example in

01:29:46.124 --> 01:29:47.762
the history of Freddy Krueger's tongue.

01:29:47.826 --> 01:29:50.978
It is again Dylan who comes to the rescue, pinning down the devil's tongue

01:29:50.994 --> 01:29:54.246
with a knife, allowing the two of them to team up and push him into the fire

01:29:54.348 --> 01:29:55.590
once and for all.

01:29:55.660 --> 01:29:58.698
As they crank up the flames with this lever, we can see the result of

01:29:58.704 --> 01:30:00.342
Dylan's attack on Krueger's tongue.

01:30:00.406 --> 01:30:03.446
It gives him a forked tongue, a trait shared with many serpents.

01:30:03.478 --> 01:30:06.582
And of course, another attribute commonly associated with the devil.

01:30:06.646 --> 01:30:09.886
The devil that took the form of Freddy Krueger to come into our world would

01:30:09.908 --> 01:30:13.470
end up sharing the same fate as the character he so closely identified with.

01:30:13.540 --> 01:30:17.562
And in his final moments, we can see him transform into his true demonic form.

01:30:17.626 --> 01:30:21.358
But we've seen Freddy killed so many times in the dream world, in the movies,

01:30:21.364 --> 01:30:24.130
only for him to come back and back and back.

01:30:24.200 --> 01:30:27.586
Who's to say that the same won't happen with the true dream demon, the one

01:30:27.608 --> 01:30:30.370
rooted in reality? I think there's a clue about his future.

01:30:30.440 --> 01:30:33.734
When Heather and Dylan reawaken to the real world and Heather finds the

01:30:33.772 --> 01:30:36.418
finished script to the movie that Wes Craven had been writing.

01:30:36.514 --> 01:30:39.320
-[Wes] Thanks for having the guts to play Nancy one last time.

01:30:39.690 --> 01:30:42.226
-[Wes] At last, Freddy's back where he belongs.

01:30:42.418 --> 01:30:44.306
-[Wes] Regards, Wes.

01:30:44.418 --> 01:30:47.766
Going off the lore that Wes had provided earlier, which has proven to be accurate.

01:30:47.788 --> 01:30:51.178
Capturing Freddy in a story will neutralize him for some time.

01:30:51.264 --> 01:30:53.994
-[Wes] Every so often, they imagine a story good enough to sort of catch its essence,

01:30:54.032 --> 01:30:56.794
-[Wes] and then for a while, it's held prisoner.

01:30:56.842 --> 01:31:01.182
-[Wes] In the story, however it happens, when the story dies, the evil is set free.

01:31:01.236 --> 01:31:05.120
And now with no new Nightmare on Elm Street for nearly 30 years.

01:31:06.450 --> 01:31:08.990
Are you sure about that? We don't talk about that.

01:31:09.060 --> 01:31:12.850
I think it's only a matter of time before the evil is set free once more.

01:31:12.920 --> 01:31:16.210
In the original iteration of Freddy Krueger, it was the fear of the children

01:31:16.280 --> 01:31:20.034
that kept him alive and in our world, not the New Nightmare world, but in

01:31:20.072 --> 01:31:21.010
our real world.

01:31:21.080 --> 01:31:24.354
The legacy of these films has kept the fear of Freddy alive for several generations,

01:31:24.402 --> 01:31:27.878
and I can only imagine that he'll continue to haunt the

01:31:27.884 --> 01:31:30.454
nightmares of many generations more.

01:31:30.572 --> 01:31:33.782
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

01:31:33.836 --> 01:31:38.054
Ring the Deathbell for all notifications, and I will see you in the next one.

01:31:38.092 --> 01:31:40.290
Assuming we both survive.

